/* 横向卡 · 第三科（分子生物学）第一张
   这两个分子到底有没有接触 —— 八种方法，八种读出。
   出处是《现代分子生物学》第五版 §6.3（印刷页 219–228），经 20260828_molecure_lite/data/
   spine_ch6_interactions.js 转录（节点 M-6-3，18 步）。那份转录自己分两层：
   正文来自扫描页；标了 beyond:true 的是通用知识，转录者注明「那一页上没写」。
   卡上凡是来自 beyond 的，当场标了「书上没写」。
   ⚠ 这张卡是她自己说的重心：「主要还是方法论吧」（2026-09-20）。
   理由是考官顺着她的课题往下追，最容易落在「你怎么证明它们结合」。
   接卡 02（Kd，SPR 和 pull-down 给的那个量）、pe-pur（抗体、标签、球珠、洗脱）、
   pe-evo（噬菌体展示的亲和力 vs 亲合力）、x-trans（报告基因、转录激活）、
   14（转化/转染，把载体弄进细胞）、16（基因组上的位置）。
   页码用 <span class="pg"> 标印刷页，例如 p.221。
   ⚠ 图：《现代分子生物学》的扫描件不在这个仓库里，只有转录出来的文字。
   图 6-18 到 6-30 都没法裁，按规矩 R4「要画的先记下不要画」，一张都没放。
   想要的图记在 LOGIC.md §16。 */

window.CARDS.push({
id:'mb-int', cross:1, w:0,
q:'这两个分子到底有没有接触 —— 八种方法，八种读出',
qcn:'横向卡 · 第三科第一张 · 脊梁：接触本身看不见，每种方法都在接触的下游造一个信号，再拿这个信号报告接触',
sub:'跨题共用 · 出处《现代分子生物学》第五版 §6.3 · 接卡 02、pe-pur、pe-evo、x-trans、14',

cram:[
 {g:'开口 · 先把八种方法串成一句话', gn:'这张卡不是八个名字的清单。它是<b>三个问题</b>，任何一种方法都能被这三个问题安放进去，名字只是填进去的例子。'},

 {n:'01', t:'这是一件什么工作',
  ez:'“Two molecules touching is not something a microscope resolves. So every method here does the same thing. It builds a signal downstream of the contact. Then it reports that signal instead. A contact is read out as a colony that grows. Or a colony that turns blue. Or an angle of reflected light. Or a band on a gel. Or a wavelength of emitted light. It is never read out as seeing the two molecules together.”',
  ezcn:'<b>两个分子有没有接触，显微镜分辨不出来。</b><b>所以这里每一种方法做的都是同一件事：在接触事件的下游造一个信号，然后拿那个信号来报告</b>。<b>「接触」被读成的东西是：一个长出来的菌落、一个变蓝的菌落、一个反射光的角度、一条胶上的带、一个新的发射波长</b>——<b>从来不是「看见两个分子在一起」。</b>',
  big:'显微镜分辨不出「两个分子在接触」。所以<b>每一种方法都在接触的下游造一个信号</b>，然后拿那个信号当答案',
  en:'“Two molecules touching is not something a microscope resolves. Every method here builds a signal downstream of the contact and reports that signal instead. A contact is read out as a colony that grows, a colony that turns blue, an angle of reflected light, a band on a gel, or a wavelength of emitted light. It is never read out as seeing the two molecules together.”',
  note:'<b>这一句是整张卡的地基，第一句就说它。</b><span class="pg">p.219</span><br>说了这一句，后面每一种方法你都只需要补三样：<b>读出是什么、在哪儿做、它看不见什么</b>。<br><b>为什么这句话值钱</b>：考官问「你怎么证明它们结合」的时候，他真正在听的是你知不知道<b>你手上那个信号离真正的接触有多远</b>。一上来就承认「我看的是下游信号」，比说「我看到它们结合了」稳得多。'},

 {n:'02', t:'三个问题，安放任何一种方法',
  ez:'“An interaction method is an experiment. It asks whether two molecules touch. I sort these methods by three questions. Which pair is being asked about. Where the experiment happens. And what the readout is. Take yeast one hybrid. It asks about a protein and a piece of D N A. It happens inside a yeast nucleus. And it reads out a blue colony. Take surface plasmon resonance. It asks about two proteins. It happens on a chip. And it reads out an angle. Once I have those three answers, I can say one more thing. I can say what that method cannot show.”',
  ezcn:'<b>我用三个问题给这些方法分类：问的是哪一对？在哪儿做？读出是什么？</b><b>酵母单杂交：问的是一个蛋白和一段 DNA，在酵母细胞核里做，读出是一个蓝色菌落。</b><b>SPR：问的是两个蛋白，在芯片上做，读出是一个角度。</b><b>三个答案一到手，我就能再说一件事：这个方法显示不出什么。</b>',
  big:'<b>问的是哪一对</b>（蛋白–DNA / 蛋白–蛋白 / RNA–RNA）· <b>在哪儿做</b>（酵母核 / 试管 / 芯片 / 活细胞）· <b>读出是什么</b>（菌落 / 条带 / 角度 / 波长 / 测序）',
  en:'“An interaction method is an experiment that asks whether two molecules touch. I sort these methods by three questions. Which pair is being asked about. Where the experiment happens. And what the readout is. Yeast one-hybrid asks about a protein and a piece of DNA, inside a yeast nucleus, and reads out a blue colony. Surface plasmon resonance asks about two proteins, on a chip, and reads out an angle. Once I have those three answers for a method I can say what it cannot show. The full account of one-hybrid is further down this card, and so is the one for surface plasmon resonance.”',
  note:'<b>这三个问题是背这张卡的唯一办法。</b>八个名字硬背会串，三个问题填空不会。<br><b>碰到一个你没见过的方法怎么办</b>：照样问这三句。他要是提一个卡上没有的方法（酵母三杂交、EMSA、DNase I 足迹法、RIP），你说 “I would ask the same three questions about it” 然后现场推，比承认没听过强得多。<br>⚠ <b>那四个方法这张卡上没有</b>，因为转录的那几页上没有；<b>别假装它们在书里</b>。'},

 {n:'03', t:'⚠ 每一种都有它显示不出来的东西',
  ez:'“Each method has something it structurally cannot show. The blind spot decides what a positive result is worth. A yeast two hybrid hit says one thing. Two proteins bind when both are put in a yeast nucleus. A co precipitation says another. Two proteins sit in one pellet. An absent F R E T signal fits two cases. Two proteins that never bind. And two that bind in the wrong orientation. So I would not claim more than the readout gives me.”',
  ezcn:'<b>每一种方法都有它结构上显示不出来的东西，而这个盲点决定了一个阳性结果值多少钱。</b><b>双杂交阳性说的是：这两个蛋白被放进同一个酵母核里会结合。</b><b>共沉淀说的是：这两个蛋白在同一个沉淀里。</b><b>没有 FRET 信号同时符合两种情况：从不结合，以及结合了但取向不对。</b><b>所以我不会说得比读出信号给我的更多。</b>',
  big:'一个方法的<b>盲点</b>，决定了它给出的阳性结果<b>值多少钱</b>。这是他插刀最狠的地方',
  en:'“Each method has something it structurally cannot show. The blind spot of a method is the part that decides what a positive result is worth. A yeast two-hybrid hit says two proteins bind when both are placed in a yeast nucleus. A co-precipitation says two proteins sit in one pellet. An absent FRET signal is consistent with two proteins that never bind and also with two that bind in the wrong orientation. I would not claim more than the readout gives me.”',
  note:'<b>这一点单独列出来，因为它是这张卡上最容易加分也最容易失分的地方。</b><br>她 2026-09-01 的 PESB 口试复盘（见 <code>LOGIC.md</code>）里，失分最重的一刀不是不知道，是<b>答的那一层不是他问的那一层</b>。这里同理：他问 “How do you know they interact?”，你答一个方法名，他下一句必然是 “And what would that experiment miss?”。<br><b>主动说出盲点，比被他挖出来好。</b>',
  warn:'⚠ <b>八分答案是「方法 ＋ 读出 ＋ 盲点」三件套，说完就停。</b>不要一口气把八种都背出来——他没问你要清单，而且背完你就把自己推到了下一层。'},

 {g:'在酵母细胞里做 · 两种（单杂交、双杂交）', gn:'这两种共用<b>同一套零件</b>：一个转录激活结构域、一个报告基因。差别只在<b>谁是已知的那一半</b>。'},

 {n:'04', t:'酵母单杂交 · 哪个蛋白结合这段 DNA',
  big:'把<b>已知的那段 DNA</b> 接在<b>最小启动子 Pmin</b>（剥到只剩核心：起始位点 ＋ TATA，<b>自己点不着火</b>）上游，报告基因接在下游，待测蛋白融合到 <b>AD</b> 上。蛋白一结合，就把 AD 拖到了 Pmin 跟前',
  en:'“Yeast one-hybrid identifies a protein that binds stably to a known piece of DNA, and it works inside a living yeast cell. A known cis-acting element is cloned upstream of a minimal promoter called Pmin, and a reporter gene is joined downstream of Pmin. A minimal promoter is one stripped back to its core, the start site and the TATA box, and on its own it is too weak to fire. That weakness is the whole point. The only thing that can switch it on is an activation domain brought to it. The candidate protein is expressed as a fusion with a yeast transcription activation domain. A protein that binds the element drags its attached activation domain to Pmin, Pmin fires, and the reporter gene is transcribed. So binding to a piece of DNA is read out as expression of a reporter gene.”',
  note:'<b>顺式作用元件（cis-acting element）＝ 调控蛋白所结合的那一小段 DNA</b>。这个词承重，必须在同一句里交代掉。<span class="pg">p.219–220（图 6-18）</span><br><b>报告基因一般是 HIS3 或 LacZ</b>，大多数体系里它待在质粒上，不整合进酵母染色体。<b>顺式元件连 3 个以上拷贝，识别和结合效率会提高</b>。<br><b>书上的实例</b>：4 个 DRE 元件排在 Pmin 上游驱动 LacZ，拟南芥 cDNA 文库融合在载有 LEU2 的载体上的 GAL4 AD 前面。<span class="pg">p.220（图 6-19）</span>',
  good:'<b>这个方法真正的用武之地是灵敏度</b>：细胞里含量低到任何生化纯化都够不着的转录调控因子，靠它能克隆出来。<b>这一句比背流程有用</b>——它回答的是「为什么不直接把蛋白纯化出来」。'},

 {n:'05', t:'⚠ 蓝色菌落是验证的起点，不是结论',
  big:'平板上变蓝的转化体被当作阳性克隆挑出来，<b>每一个都还要再测序、再单独验证结合活性</b>',
  en:'“Yeast transformants that turn blue are picked as positive clones. Every one of them is then sequenced and has its binding activity verified separately. A blue colony is where the verification starts.”',
  note:'<b>这句是书上自己写的，不是我加的限定。</b><span class="pg">p.220</span><br>为什么要强调：一个文库筛选出来的阳性，<b>本身是一个候选，不是一个答案</b>。她答「我做了单杂交，筛到了」，考官接 “And then?”——答不上来这一步，前面说得再顺也停在半路。'},

 {n:'06', t:'整套读出的支点 · 转录调控因子是组件式的',
  big:'真核转录调控因子由<b>相互独立的结构域</b>拼成，激活因子必需的是两个：<b>DNA 结合结构域 BD</b> 和<b>转录激活结构域 AD</b>。两者要到同一个位置，<b>但不必长在同一条多肽链上</b>',
  en:'“Eukaryotic transcription regulators have a modular structure. Each one is built from two or more mutually independent domains, and an activator needs two of them in order to work. One is a DNA binding domain and the other is an activation domain. A binding domain on its own binds the promoter region of a gene and stops there, having started no transcription. A hybrid protein carrying the binding domain of one regulator and the activation domain of a different regulator activates transcription perfectly well. So the two domains have to arrive in the same place, and they do not have to be on the same polypeptide.”',
  note:'<b>这一点是整组的支点，单杂交和双杂交都是从它长出来的。</b><span class="pg">p.221</span><br>把这一句说清楚，后面双杂交你不用解释原理，一句 “that separation put to work on protein pairs” 就够了。<br><b>同一个事实还有第二种用法</b>：把某个未知基因融合到 GAL4 的 BD 上，去读 GAL4 顺式元件下游的报告基因；报告基因亮了，说明<b>这个未知蛋白自身带有转录激活功能</b>。这是一个独立的实验，不是双杂交。',
  good:'<b>接卡 x-trans</b>：那张卡讲的是「从基因到蛋白，细胞把同一条信息抄两遍」。这里用到的是抄第一遍那一步的开关——<b>转录激活</b>。报告基因能亮，说明 RNA 聚合酶被招来了。'},

 {n:'07', t:'酵母双杂交 · 诱饵和猎物',
  big:'BD 挂<b>已知蛋白</b>＝诱饵（bait），AD 挂 <b>cDNA 文库的每个插入片段</b>＝猎物（prey）。猎物一结合诱饵，AD 和 BD 被牵到一起，凑成一个能干活的转录调控因子',
  en:'“Yeast two-hybrid is that separation of the two domains put to work on protein pairs. The sequence of a known protein is joined to the binding domain fragment of a yeast regulator such as GAL4 on an expression vector. The hybrid protein binds the regulatory region upstream of a reporter gene and sits there. That construct is the bait, meaning the half that is known and fixed. The activation domain fragment is joined separately to each insert of a cDNA library to give prey vectors, and those are transformed into the bait carrying cells. When a prey protein binds the bait, the two domains are drawn together into one working regulator, the reporter gene switches on, and the prey vector recovered from that colony carries a new interacting gene.”',
  note:'<b>常用的 BD 来源是 GAL1、GAL4 或 GCN1。</b><span class="pg">p.221（图 6-20）</span><br><b>「诱饵」这个词的定义要说出来</b>：bait ＝ 已知的、固定不动的那一半。不说清楚，他会以为你在背比喻。<br><b>拿回来的是什么</b>：一个菌落 → 回收猎物载体 → 里面那段 cDNA 就是一个新的互作基因。<b>整个筛选的产物是一段序列，不是一个结论。</b>',
  good:'<b>接卡 14</b>：「转化进含诱饵的酵母细胞」用的就是那张卡上的 transformation。酵母是转化，不是转染——<b>这两个词说反是实测会被抓的。</b>'},

 {n:'08', t:'⚠ 双杂交的盲点 · 它要求的条件就是它的限制',
  big:'两边都得<b>在酵母里被造出来</b>、都<b>进得了酵母核</b>、还得<b>结合得够久</b>让报告基因转录完。<b>这三条要求，同时就是三个盲点</b>',
  en:'“Both partners have to be produced inside a yeast cell, reach the yeast nucleus, and hold together long enough for a reporter gene to be transcribed. Two consequences follow. An interaction that depends on a chemical modification yeast does not make will not appear at all. And two proteins that are never in the same compartment in the organism they came from can still score positive. A yeast two-hybrid hit is a statement about two proteins placed together in a yeast nucleus. It carries no information about whether those two ever meet in the cell they came from.”',
  note:'<b>最后那一句是这一点的八分答案，说完就停。</b><span class="pg">p.221</span><br>⚠ <b>书上没写</b>：那两个后果是从机制推出来的通用知识，转录者标了 <code>beyond</code>，说那一页上只有机制和读出。<b>说的时候别挂到书上</b>，说 “that follows from how the assay works” 就对了。<br><b>两个后果各自对应什么</b>：<b>假阴性</b>＝依赖磷酸化、糖基化这类酵母做不出的修饰的互作，根本不出现；<b>假阳性</b>＝原本一个在核里一个在膜上、永不相遇的两个蛋白，在这里照样阳性。'},

 {g:'从细胞里拿出来做 · 三种（SPR、CoIP、GST pull-down）', gn:'这三种都在试管或芯片上。共同的好处是<b>能给一个量</b>，共同的代价是<b>诱饵不在细胞里了</b>。'},

 {n:'09', t:'SPR · 等离子体表面共振',
  big:'诱饵固定在<b>纳米厚金属膜</b>上的葡聚糖层里，蛋白混合物流过。凡是结合上的，<b>都让表面折射率上升，反射光的共振角度跟着变</b>',
  en:'“Surface plasmon resonance immobilises the bait protein on a dextran layer, and that layer is fixed onto a metal film of nanometre thickness. A protein mixture is flowed past it. Anything in the mixture that interacts with the bait raises the refractive index at the film surface, and that shifts the resonance angle. The resonance angle is the angle at which the reflected light loses intensity, and the shift is linear in the protein concentration at that spot. Surface plasmon resonance needs no label and no dye. It is fast and it returns a quantity rather than a yes. The price is a dedicated instrument, and a bait sitting on a chip instead of in a cell.”',
  note:'<b>共振角度＝反射光强度下降的那个角度</b>。这个词承重，一句话交代掉。<span class="pg">p.221–222（图 6-21）</span><br><b>SPR 在八种里的位置</b>：它是<b>最物理的那一端</b>。上一组读的是「报告基因转录了没有」，隔着好几层；这里读的是一个角度，中间没有生物学。<br><b>无标记、无染料</b>这一点要说，因为它直接回答「你的标签会不会干扰结合」。',
  good:'<b>接卡 02</b>：SPR 给的正是那张卡上的<b>结合曲线</b>。<b>她的主场在这里</b>——K<sub>d</sub> 那张卡讲的是这个量怎么定义、怎么被误读；这张卡讲的是这个量在实验台上从哪儿来。'},

 {n:'10', t:'SPR 的实例 · 一对蛋白还需要第三个分子',
  big:'JAZ1 以 <b>1000 共振单位</b>固定在芯片上。<b>只有体系里同时有 JA–Ile 时，COI1 才结合</b>（升到 380 单位）；单独的 COI1 贴着零',
  en:'“JAZ1 is a negative regulator of the jasmonic acid signalling pathway, and it was immobilised on the chip at one thousand resonance units. With jasmonic acid isoleucine and COI1 both present, the signal climbed to three hundred and eighty resonance units. Luciferase, luciferase with the small molecule, and COI1 on its own all stayed near zero. Coronatine is a bacterial toxin resembling methyl jasmonate, and it drove the same interaction to about three hundred and ten units, while three other related small molecules produced no response. So COI1 binds JAZ1 only when a particular small molecule is present as well, and a trace measured in resonance units is what turns that requirement into a number.”',
  note:'<b>这个例子值得记，因为它回答的是一个很常见的追问</b>：「你做了实验没看到结合，能说明它们不结合吗」。<b>不能</b>——可能缺一个小分子。<span class="pg">p.222（图 6-22）</span><br><b>三条对照都贴零</b>：荧光素酶、荧光素酶加 JA–Ile、单独 COI1。<b>对照是这个实验的全部说服力所在</b>。<br>⚠ <b>数字别记混</b>：固定量 1000 单位是<b>芯片上装了多少诱饵</b>，380 是<b>结合信号的高度</b>，约 350 s 处那个是<b>解离尖峰</b>。三个数三件事。<br>COR ＝ 冠毒素，细菌毒素，结构和功能都像茉莉酸甲酯（MeJA）；无反应的三个是 JA、MeJA 和 OPDA。'},

 {n:'11', t:'免疫共沉淀 CoIP · 全部读出就是「在不在沉淀里」',
  big:'靶蛋白的<b>抗体</b>连在固体基质上，加待筛选蛋白，<b>低速离心</b>；基质、抗体和挂在它们身上的一切一起沉到管底',
  en:'“Co-immunoprecipitation rests on one thing, an antibody specific for the target protein. That antibody is coupled by an affinity reaction onto a solid matrix. The proteins to be screened are added to the system, and low centrifugal force or microfiltration brings the matrix, the antibody and everything hanging off them down to the bottom of the tube. A screened protein that has interacted with the target rides down attached to it. So presence in the pellet is the entire readout of the experiment.”',
  note:'<b>「全部读出就是在不在沉淀里」——这句话本身就是盲点的伏笔</b>，先说出来，下一点接得上。<span class="pg">p.222–223（图 6-23）</span><br><b>关键词是低速</b>：low centrifugal force。转速高了复合物会被打散，也会把不相干的东西一起沉下来。<br><b>接卡 pe-pur</b>：那张卡上的亲和纯化用的是同一套逻辑——<b>把一样东西固定住，让它去抓别的</b>。差别只在抓手是抗体还是镍离子。'},

 {n:'12', t:'CoIP 实操 · 两个标签，一张胶',
  big:'两个靶蛋白由 <b>pGADT7</b> 和 <b>pGBKT7</b> 表达成融合蛋白，一个带 <b>HA 标签</b>一个带 <b>c-Myc 标签</b>。<b>用 Myc 抗体沉淀，然后看同一条泳道里有没有 HA 那一个</b>',
  en:'“In practice neither protein is chased with an antibody of its own. Each is expressed as a fusion carrying a short tag that a ready made antibody recognises. One carries an HA tag and the other carries a c-Myc tag. Both are transcribed and translated in vitro, the products are mixed and incubated, the mixture is precipitated with either antibody, passed over a column, and separated by gel electrophoresis. Whether the two proteins interact is read straight off that gel. Precipitate with the Myc antibody, then look for the HA tagged partner in the same lane.”',
  note:'<b>标签＝一小段有现成抗体认得的多肽序列。</b>这个词承重，交代掉。<span class="pg">p.223（图 6-24）</span><br><b>为什么用标签不用各自的抗体</b>：做一支特异抗体既慢又贵，而且对没研究过的蛋白根本没有现成的。<b>标签把「要一支新抗体」变成「用一支旧抗体」。</b><br><b>体外转录翻译</b>：两边都是在管子里做出来的，不在细胞里。<b>接卡 pe-cfps</b>，那张卡讲的就是把翻译搬进管子。<br>书上的实例是六对：棉花乙烯合成酶 <b>ACS2 与钙依赖蛋白激酶 CDPK1 是唯一的阳性</b>；ACS2 对 CDPK32、CRK5 都没有；ACO1 对三个都没有。<b>每对跑 H 和 c 两条泳道，c 是共沉淀那一份</b>；ACO1 底下 c 泳道空、H 泳道还有带——<b>这就是这里的阴性长什么样</b>。<span class="pg">p.223–224（图 6-25）</span>'},

 {n:'13', t:'⚠ CoIP 的盲点 · 同一个复合物不等于彼此接触',
  big:'共沉淀说明两个蛋白<b>在同一个被沉下来的复合物里</b>。至于是<b>彼此直接接触</b>，还是<b>同时被第三样东西攥着</b>，<b>这张胶分不开</b>',
  en:'“A co-precipitation puts two proteins in one pelleted complex. Whether they touch each other, or are both held by a third thing in the mixture, is a question the gel does not separate.”',
  note:'⚠ <b>书上没写</b>：这一条转录者标了 <code>beyond</code>，说印刷页 223 到 224 上有配对、结论和那条空泳道，但这句关于「复合物不等于接触」的话不在那两页上。<b>说的时候标明它是通用知识。</b><br><b>怎么补救这个盲点</b>（他很可能追这一句）：<b>做体外的重组蛋白 pull-down</b>（只有两个纯化出来的蛋白，没有第三者），或者<b>用 FRET 看距离</b>（1 到 10 纳米是直接接触的尺度）。<b>这一句把这张卡自己串起来了</b>——一个方法的盲点，正好是另一个方法的强项。',
  warn:'⚠ <b>这是最容易被抓的一刀。</b>说「CoIP 证明 A 和 B 相互作用」——他接 “Directly?” 你就停住了。<b>正确说法是 “they are in the same complex”。</b>'},

 {n:'14', t:'GST pull-down · 对照管才是让胶可读的东西',
  big:'GST 对球珠上的<b>谷胱甘肽</b>有亲和性。一管放 <b>GST–蛋白X ＋ 裂解物</b>，对照管放<b>裸 GST ＋ 同样的裂解物</b>。<b>只在前一管出现的那条带，才是 X 的互作蛋白</b>',
  en:'“A pull-down is a purification with a handle. Glutathione S-transferase has affinity for glutathione coupled to agarose beads, so anything fused to it can be fished out of a mixed protein sample. One tube receives the fusion of the tag with protein X, the beads, and a labelled cell lysate. A control tube receives bare tag with the same beads and the same lysate. After incubation at four degrees and a spin, the first tube yields beads with the fusion and whatever partner it held, and the second yields beads with the bare tag alone. Gel electrophoresis resolves three bands. A band present with the fusion and absent with the bare tag is what identifies a partner of X. So the control tube is what makes the gel readable at all.”',
  note:'<b>三条带自上而下</b>：发生相互作用的蛋白质、GST 融合物、GST。<span class="pg">p.223–224（图 6-26）</span><br><b>裂解物是 ³⁵S 标记的</b>，所以胶上读的是放射性信号。<br><b>4 ℃ 反应</b>：低温减少蛋白降解，也让弱的结合不容易散。<br><b>接卡 pe-pur</b>：GST 是那张卡上的<b>亲和标签</b>之一。<b>同一个 GST，在纯化那张卡上是为了把目标蛋白弄干净，在这张卡上是为了钓出别人。</b>标签一样，问题不一样。',
  good:'<b>「对照管才是让这张胶可读的东西」——这句话可以单独拿出来用。</b>他要是问「你怎么设计一个互作实验」，这一句比任何流程都像一个做过实验的人说的。'},

 {n:'15', t:'pull-down 给的是百分数，不是判决',
  big:'PIF3 做钓饵：<b>超过 30% 的 phyB</b> 被沉下来；<b>缺了 N 端 37 个氨基酸的 phyB 突变体约 10%</b>；phyA 约 5%；单独的 GAD 接近零',
  en:'“The same layout was run with a GAL4 activation domain fused to different segments of PIF3 as the bait, against phytochrome prey. Over thirty percent of phytochrome B was precipitated. A mutant of phytochrome B lacking its amino terminal thirty seven residues gave about ten percent. Phytochrome A gave about five percent, and the tag on its own gave close to zero. A pull-down returns a percentage rather than a verdict. So deleting thirty seven residues shows up as a fall from thirty percent to ten percent, instead of as an interaction that vanishes.”',
  note:'<b>和 SPR 的共振单位是同一招：给一个数，而不只给一个「有」。</b><span class="pg">p.223, p.225（图 6-27）</span><br><b>为什么这一点重要</b>：定量的读出能让你看见<b>「弱化」</b>，而不只是<b>「消失」</b>。删掉 37 个残基，互作从 30% 掉到 10%——这句话说明那 37 个残基参与但不是全部。<b>定性的实验给不出这个结论。</b><br><b>接卡 02</b>：这正是 K<sub>d</sub> 那张卡的精神——<b>结合不是有和无，是强和弱</b>。'},

 {g:'在活细胞里做 · 两种（FRET、ChIP）', gn:'前面两组要么把分子搬进酵母，要么把它拿出细胞。<b>这两种不搬</b>，代价各自不同。'},

 {n:'16', t:'FRET · 三个条件必须同时满足',
  big:'蛋白 A 接 <b>CFP</b>，蛋白 B 接 <b>YFP</b>。两者靠近时，<b>440 nm 激发给出的从 CFP 的 480 nm 换成 YFP 的 535 nm</b>。条件是：<b>相距 1–10 nm · 光谱有重叠 · 偶极取向合适</b>',
  en:'“Fluorescence resonance energy transfer is energy passing from a fluorescent donor to a fluorescent acceptor by dipole coupling, without radiation. It needs three conditions at once. The donor and acceptor must be one to ten nanometres apart. The emission spectrum of the donor must overlap the absorption spectrum of the acceptor. And the two dipoles must be in a suitable spatial orientation. Protein A carries cyan fluorescent protein and protein B carries yellow fluorescent protein. Held apart, they give only the four hundred and eighty nanometre emission of the donor under excitation at four hundred and forty. Brought together by an interaction, the same excitation yields the five hundred and thirty five nanometre emission of the acceptor, and fluorescence imaging records that colour change inside the cell.”',
  note:'<b>三个条件是这一点的全部。</b>说出来的时候按 <b>距离 → 光谱 → 取向</b> 这个顺序，最好记。<span class="pg">p.225–226（图 6-28）</span><br><b>1 到 10 纳米这个尺度要记住</b>：它就是「直接接触」的物理尺度。这也是为什么 FRET 能补 CoIP 的盲点。<br><b>非辐射</b>：能量不是先发出一个光子再被吸收，是直接通过偶极耦合传过去的。这个词他可能单独问。'},

 {n:'17', t:'⚠ 没有 FRET 信号，不等于不结合',
  big:'三个条件里<b>任何一个不满足</b>，535 nm 都不出现。所以「没有 FRET」对<b>「从不结合」</b>和<b>「结合了但取向不对」</b>同样成立',
  en:'“Any one of the three conditions failing leaves no acceptor signal. So an absent FRET result is equally consistent with two proteins that never bind, and with two proteins that bind in the wrong orientation.”',
  note:'<b>这是全卡最干净的一个阴性陷阱，一定要会说。</b><span class="pg">p.226</span><br><b>为什么它特别容易被问</b>：阴性结果的解释是口试里最能分出「做过」和「背过」的地方。背过的人说「没有相互作用」，做过的人说「我的实验没检出」。<br><b>怎么补</b>：换标签在蛋白上的位置（N 端换到 C 端），取向变了信号可能就出来了。<b>这一句说出来非常加分</b>，因为它说明你知道 FRET 测的是几何而不只是接触。'},

 {n:'18', t:'ChIP · 这个蛋白结合基因组上的哪些地方',
  big:'和单杂交<b>正好反过来</b>。单杂交问「哪个蛋白结合这段 DNA」，ChIP 问「<b>这个蛋白结合哪些 DNA</b>」。五步：<b>活细胞固定 → 随机打断 → 抗体沉淀 → 纯化加接头 → 高通量测序</b>',
  en:'“Chromatin immunoprecipitation asks the reverse of the one-hybrid question. One-hybrid asks which protein binds a chosen piece of DNA. This asks which DNA a chosen protein binds, and it asks it inside a living cell. The procedure has five moves. Protein and DNA complexes are fixed while the cells are alive. Sonication or enzyme treatment cuts the chromatin randomly into small fragments. An antibody precipitates the complex and enriches the DNA fragments bound to the protein of interest. Those fragments are purified, end repaired and given adaptors. And high throughput sequencing reads them. What comes out is the sequence of the bound DNA, its position in the genome, the strength of binding, and its effect on gene expression.”',
  note:'<b>五步要背顺序，顺序本身就是答案的骨架。</b><span class="pg">p.226–227（图 6-29、6-30）</span><br><b>「活细胞状态下固定」是第一步，也是整个方法成立的原因</b>：先把接触冻住，再去拆细胞。顺序反了就什么都测不到。<br><b>接卡 16</b>：那张卡讲 DNA 复制，用到的是同一个概念——<b>基因组上的位置</b>。'},

 {n:'19', t:'ChIP 的分辨率 · 定位到一段染色质，不是一个碱基',
  big:'ChIP 交还给你的是<b>一段有一定长度的片段</b>。所以它把蛋白定位到<b>染色质的一段上</b>，不是定位到某一个碱基上',
  en:'“Chromatin immunoprecipitation hands back a fragment of a certain length. So it places a protein on a stretch of chromatin, rather than on a base.”',
  note:'<b>这一句是它的盲点，也是它和足迹法之类方法的分界。</b><span class="pg">p.227</span><br><b>抗体不必针对转录因子</b>：换成针对组蛋白共价修饰的抗体，它就能测这种修饰的分布和基因表达的关系。<b>棉花里用抗 H3K4me3 抗体做全基因组检测</b>，富集轨迹上<b>约 31 和约 23 两个峰</b>正落在 Cotton_A_37370 和 Cotton_A_37371 两个基因的 <b>5′ 端</b>，<b>基因体中部几乎为零</b>。<span class="pg">p.226–227（图 6-30）</span><br><b>那两个峰落在 5′ 端这件事本身就是结论</b>：H3K4me3 标记的是活跃基因的启动子区。',
  good:'<b>一句很值钱的收尾</b>：把目的蛋白定位到某个<b>具体基因的启动子区</b>，这一步才是把一次结合测量<b>变成一句关于这个蛋白生物学功能的论断</b>。测到结合是数据，落到某个基因上才是结果。'},

 {g:'RNA 对 RNA · 一种（RNAi）', gn:'这一串里最后一种相互作用不在蛋白之间。它也不是<b>检测</b>方法，是<b>扰动</b>方法——<b>这个区别本身就是一道题</b>。'},

 {n:'20', t:'RNAi · 用双链小 RNA 降解同源 mRNA',
  big:'<b>dsRNA 是触发物</b>，触发的是与它互补的那条单链 RNA 被降解。<b>Dicer</b>（有 RNase Ⅲ 活性的核酸酶）把 30 nt 以上的 dsRNA 切成 <b>21–25 nt 的 siRNA</b>',
  en:'“RNA interference uses a small double stranded RNA to degrade the homologous messenger RNA inside a cell, efficiently and specifically. It blocks expression of the target gene, so the cell shows the phenotype of having lost that gene. The first observation was in a nematode. Foreign double stranded RNA injected into the worm induced specific silencing of gene sequences highly homologous to that RNA. Double stranded RNA is the trigger, and what it triggers is degradation of the single stranded RNA complementary to it. Dicer is a nuclease with RNase three activity, and it cuts double stranded RNA longer than thirty nucleotides into short interfering RNA of twenty one to twenty five nucleotides. Double stranded RNA too short to be processed into that size cannot mediate interference at all.”',
  note:'<b>最早在线虫里看到</b>，后来在果蝇、锥虫、涡虫和大部分植物里都找到了。<span class="pg">p.226–228</span><br><b>21–25 nt 这个数字要记住</b>，它在下一点还要用一次（哺乳动物细胞里的特异性）。<br><b>siRNA 的结构特征</b>：<b>5′ 端磷酸基团、3′ 端羟基，两条链的 3′ 端各有两个碱基突出</b>。这个结构他可能单独问。'},

 {n:'21', t:'RISC 和 RdRP · 一条 siRNA 同时给了切割装置和扩增办法',
  big:'siRNA 的<b>反义链</b>指导装配 <b>RISC</b>，由它切开目的 mRNA 上互补的那一段。同时 <b>RdRP</b> 以同一条 mRNA 为模板造出新的 dsRNA，<b>再切成新的 siRNA 重新进入循环</b>',
  en:'“The antisense strand of the small interfering RNA directs assembly of a ribonucleoprotein called the RNA induced silencing complex. That complex cleaves the region of the target message complementary to the antisense strand. The small RNA also doubles as a special primer. An RNA dependent RNA polymerase copies the target message into fresh double stranded RNA, which is cut into new small interfering RNA and re-enters the cycle. So even a low injected dose is amplified into complete gene silencing.”',
  note:'<b>放大这件事解释了一个常见的疑问</b>：注进去那么一点点 RNA，怎么能把整个基因关掉。<b>因为产物又变成了原料。</b><span class="pg">p.228</span><br>⚠ <b>哺乳动物细胞里的限定</b>：较长的 dsRNA 会引起<b>非特异性</b>沉默，<b>只有 21–25 nt 的 siRNA 在那里才是特异的</b>。这一条是实验设计上的真限制，值得单独说。'},

 {n:'22', t:'⚠ RNAi 和基因敲除的区别 · 一个毁信使，一个拿掉基因',
  big:'从头到尾<b>被摧毁的是 mRNA</b>，<b>靶基因本身仍然留在基因组上</b>。基因敲除是把基因从染色体上去掉',
  en:'“Throughout interference it is the messenger RNA that is destroyed, and the target gene stays in the genome. Gene knockout removes the gene from the chromosome. Interference leaves the gene and destroys its message. So interference gives a knockdown rather than a knockout, and the phenotype it produces is a reduction rather than an absence.”',
  note:'<b>这一点是这张卡和那一张方法卡（基因敲除、CRISPR）的接口。</b><br><b>为什么这个区别值钱</b>：它直接决定实验能说什么。<b>敲除给的是「没有这个基因会怎样」，RNAi 给的是「这个基因少一点会怎样」。</b>而且 RNAi 从来不是 100%，所以<b>表型弱不一定说明这个基因不重要，可能只是没敲干净</b>。<br>⚠ <b>knockdown 和 knockout 这两个词说反是实测级别的错误。</b>',
  warn:'⚠ <b>RNAi 在这一节里的位置有点特别，别被他绕进去。</b>前七种是<b>检测</b>相互作用的方法，RNAi 是<b>利用</b>一种相互作用（RNA 对 RNA）去<b>扰动</b>基因。他要是问 “Is RNAi an interaction detection method?”，老实答 “It is not a detection method, it is a perturbation method that exploits an RNA to RNA interaction.”'}
],

end:'八种方法，一个问题。<b>说的时候只给三样：这是哪一对、在哪儿做、读出是什么。</b>再加一句「它看不见什么」，就停。<b>不要背清单。</b>',

sib:[
 ['这一组方法回答的是什么问题','“Do these two molecules touch? Every method here answers that one question with a different readout.”','一句话把八个名字串起来。先说问题，再说方法，不要先报名字。'],
 ['为什么不能直接看','“A contact is not something a microscope resolves, so every method builds a signal downstream of the contact and reports that instead.”','这是整张卡的地基。说了它，后面每种方法都只需要补三样。'],
 ['安放任何一种方法的三个问题','“Which pair, where it happens, and what the readout is.”','背这张卡的唯一办法。碰到没见过的方法也照样问这三句。'],
 ['酵母单杂交问的是哪一边','“One-hybrid asks which protein binds a chosen piece of DNA. The protein drags an activation domain to a minimal promoter and a reporter gene fires.”','已知的是 DNA，未知的是蛋白。'],
 ['整套酵母读出的支点','“A hybrid protein carrying the binding domain of one regulator and the activation domain of another activates transcription perfectly well.”','两个结构域要到同一个位置，不必在同一条链上。说清楚这句，双杂交就不用再解释原理。'],
 ['酵母双杂交的盲点','“A hit says two proteins bind when both are placed in a yeast nucleus. It carries no information about whether they ever meet in the cell they came from.”','假阴性来自酵母做不出的修饰，假阳性来自原本不同区室的两个蛋白。'],
 ['SPR 强在哪','“It needs no label and no dye, and it returns a quantity rather than a yes.”','代价是专门的仪器，和一个待在芯片上而不在细胞里的诱饵。'],
 ['CoIP 能说到什么程度','“A co-precipitation puts two proteins in one pelleted complex. Whether they touch, or are both held by a third thing, is a question the gel does not separate.”','说「in the same complex」，不要说「directly interact」。'],
 ['pull-down 的对照管','“A band present with the fusion and absent with the bare tag is what identifies a partner. The control tube is what makes the gel readable at all.”','这一句比背流程更像一个做过实验的人说的。'],
 ['FRET 的三个条件','“One to ten nanometres apart, overlapping spectra, and a suitable dipole orientation. Any one of them failing leaves no signal.”','所以阴性结果不能读成「不结合」。'],
 ['ChIP 问的是哪一边','“It asks which DNA a chosen protein binds, inside a living cell, and it hands back a fragment rather than a base.”','和单杂交正好反过来。分辨率是一段染色质。'],
 ['RNAi 和敲除差在哪','“Interference destroys the message and leaves the gene in the genome. Knockout removes the gene from the chromosome.”','knockdown 不是 knockout，表型是减弱不是缺失。']
],

segs:[
 {tag:'段 1 · 定义', h:'先说这一组方法在干什么，再说为什么它们看起来这么不一样',
  p:['“Eight methods, one question. Do these two molecules touch.”',
     '“Two molecules touching is not something a microscope resolves. So every method here builds a signal downstream of the contact and reports that signal instead.”',
     '“A contact is read out as a colony that grows, a colony that turns blue, an angle of reflected light, a band on a gel, or a wavelength of emitted light. It is never read out as seeing the two molecules together.”',
     '“That is why the methods look so different from each other. They are not different answers. They are different ways of making the same event leave a mark.”'],
  note:'<b>第一句就是定义和轴，不要从背景起手。</b>「八种方法一个问题」这个开头把整段的结构先交给他，他知道你要往哪儿走。<br>最后那句是这一段的落点：<b>方法之间的差别不在结论，在读出</b>。'},

 {tag:'段 2 · 展开', h:'三个问题把八种方法排成一张表 —— 给一个他能记住的结构',
  p:['“I sort them by three questions. Which pair is being asked about. Where the experiment happens. And what the readout is.”',
     '“Two of them happen inside a yeast cell. One-hybrid asks which protein binds a chosen piece of DNA. Two-hybrid asks which protein binds a chosen protein. Both read out as a reporter gene switching on.”',
     '“Three of them take the pair out of any cell. Surface plasmon resonance reads an angle on a chip. Co-immunoprecipitation reads presence in a pellet. And a pull-down reads a band that is there with the tagged bait and absent with the bare tag.”',
     '“Two of them stay inside a living cell. Energy transfer between two fluorescent proteins reads a change of emitted wavelength. Chromatin immunoprecipitation reads a sequenced fragment of DNA.”',
     '“And the last one is not protein with protein at all. Interference exploits an RNA binding a complementary RNA, and it uses that to destroy a message.”'],
  note:'<b>四组，不是八项。</b>酵母里两种、拿出来三种、活细胞两种、RNA 一种。<b>四个数字比八个名字好记得多</b>，而且分组本身是答案的一部分——它说明你按「在哪儿做」理解这些方法。<br>⚠ 这一段说完大概 50 秒，<b>是整张卡里最可能被打断的地方</b>。被打断很正常，他打断说明他找到了想挖的那一条。'},

 {tag:'段 3 · 深一层', h:'挑一条往下挖 —— 每个方法的盲点，以及盲点之间怎么互相补',
  p:['“The useful thing about this list is not the methods. It is that each one has something it structurally cannot show.”',
     '“A two-hybrid hit says two proteins bind when both are placed in a yeast nucleus. It says nothing about whether they ever meet in the cell they came from.”',
     '“A co-precipitation puts two proteins in one pellet. Whether they touch each other, or are both held by a third thing, the gel does not separate.”',
     '“An absent energy transfer signal is equally consistent with two proteins that never bind and with two that bind in the wrong orientation.”',
     '“So I would not read any one of these as a conclusion on its own. The blind spot of one method is usually the strength of another. If a co-precipitation cannot tell me whether the contact is direct, a pull-down with two purified proteins can, and energy transfer can, because one to ten nanometres is the scale of a direct contact.”'],
  note:'<b>这一段是整张卡的核心，也是最能拉开分数的地方。</b>前两段任何背过书的人都能说，这一段只有想过的人能说。<br><b>最后一句的形状要记住</b>：先承认单个方法不够，再<b>具体说出用哪个方法补、为什么它能补</b>。空泛地说「要多种方法互相验证」是废话，说「CoIP 分不出直接还是间接，所以用纯化蛋白的 pull-down 或者 FRET，因为 1 到 10 纳米就是直接接触的尺度」才是回答。'},

 {tag:'段 4 · 落点', h:'停在一个量上 —— 这些方法里真正能定量的那几个，和她自己的主场',
  p:['“There is one more axis under all of this, and it is whether the method returns a yes or a number.”',
     '“Surface plasmon resonance returns resonance units, and a pull-down returns a percentage. Over thirty percent of one phytochrome came down with the bait, and a mutant lacking thirty seven residues gave about ten percent.”',
     '“That matters because it turns an interaction that weakens into something I can see. A qualitative assay would have shown a band in both cases.”',
     '“And a number is what lets one experiment show that a pair needs a third molecule. A plant regulator was immobilised on a chip, and its partner only bound when a particular small molecule was present in the system as well. Without a quantitative trace, that experiment reads as a failed experiment.”',
     '“So when I am asked whether two things interact, the question I actually want to answer is how tightly, and under what conditions.”'],
  note:'<b>这一段落在她的主场：结合是强和弱，不是有和无。</b>这正是卡 02（K<sub>d</sub>）的精神，也是 pe-evo 里亲和力和亲合力那一条的精神。<br><b>最后那句是停止句</b>，它把问题从「有没有」抬到「多紧、什么条件下」——<b>停在这里他很可能接着问 K<sub>d</sub>，而那张卡你是熟的。</b><br><b>这是故意的</b>：停止句要停在你还稳的地方，把下一刀引到你的主场。'}
],

why:{
 rungs:[
  ['为什么八种方法要一起记，不能只记一种？','因为<b>每一种都有它显示不出来的东西</b>，而一个方法的盲点，正好是另一个方法的强项。只会一种，就没法回答「那这个实验漏了什么」。'],
  ['为什么读出是什么这么重要？','因为<b>接触本身看不见</b>。你手上永远只有一个下游信号——菌落、条带、角度、波长。知道自己离真正的接触隔着几层，才知道这个阳性值多少钱。'],
  ['为什么酵母双杂交的阳性要打折听？','因为它要求两边都在酵母里造出来、都进核、还结合得够久。<b>这三条要求同时就是三个盲点</b>：酵母做不出的修饰导致假阴性，原本不同区室的两个蛋白导致假阳性。'],
  ['为什么定量的方法值钱？','因为它让<b>「弱化」</b>看得见。删掉 37 个残基，互作从 30% 掉到 10%——定性的实验只会告诉你两边都有带。'],
  ['为什么 RNAi 被放在这一节里？','因为它利用的也是一种分子间相互作用，<b>只不过发生在 RNA 和 RNA 之间</b>。但它是<b>扰动</b>方法不是<b>检测</b>方法——这个区别要主动说。']
 ],
 stop:{lbl:'停 · 落在「多紧、什么条件下」',
  say:'“So when I am asked whether two things interact, the question I actually want to answer is how tightly, and under what conditions.”'}
},

recog:[
 {q:'How would you show that two proteins interact?',
  ez:'“I would answer with three questions. Which pair. Where the experiment happens. And what the readout is. For a screen against a library I would use yeast two hybrid. A hit there means they bind in a yeast nucleus. For a number I would use surface plasmon resonance. A pull down also gives numbers. For an answer inside a living cell I would use energy transfer. That means two fluorescent proteins. And I would not read any single method as a conclusion.”',
  ezcn:'<b>我会用三个问题来答：哪一对 · 实验发生在哪里 · 读出是什么。</b><b>要对文库做筛选就用酵母双杂交，而且要记住「阳性」的意思是「它们在酵母细胞核里结合」；要一个数就用表面等离子共振或者 pull-down；要在活细胞里就用两个荧光蛋白之间的能量转移。</b>⚠ <b>任何单一方法都不能当结论——别一口气背八种，给结构、给两三个例子、然后停。</b>',
  mean:'这是<b>这道题的最短问法</b>，也是他最可能用的那一句。他要的是一个<b>有结构的答案</b>，不是一个方法名。',
  say:'“I would answer it with three questions. Which pair, where the experiment happens, and what the readout is. If I want a screen against a library I would use yeast two-hybrid, and I would remember that a hit means they bind in a yeast nucleus. If I want a number I would use surface plasmon resonance or a pull-down. And if I want it inside a living cell I would use energy transfer between two fluorescent proteins. I would not read any single one as a conclusion.”',
  tail:'⚠ <b>不要一口气背八种。</b>给结构、给两三个例子、给一句「单个方法不够」，然后停。'},

 {q:'How do you know they interact?',
  ez:'“With the assay I used I can say one thing. They are in the same complex. To say the contact is direct I need more. I would do a pull down with two purified proteins. Or I would measure energy transfer. Energy transfer reports one to ten nanometres. That is the scale of a direct contact.”',
  ezcn:'<b>用我做的那个实验，我能说的是：它们在同一个复合物里。</b><b>要说「直接接触」还需要多一步：用两个纯化蛋白做 pull-down，或者做能量转移测量——因为 1–10 纳米正是直接接触的尺度。</b><b>这个形状（先说这个实验能说到哪一层，再说往上一层需要什么）几乎对任何方法都适用。</b>',
  mean:'这是<b>顺着她课题往下追最常见的那一刀</b>。他不是在考方法，是在考<b>她对自己数据的信心边界</b>。',
  say:'“With the assay I used I can say they are in the same complex. To say the contact is direct I would need a pull-down with two purified proteins, or an energy transfer measurement, because one to ten nanometres is the scale of a direct contact.”',
  tail:'<b>先说这个实验能说到哪一层，再说要往上一层需要什么。</b>这个形状几乎对任何方法都适用。'},

 {q:'What is a reporter gene?',
  ez:'“A reporter gene is a gene with a product that is easy to see. It is placed downstream of the regulatory sequence being tested. So transcription of that sequence becomes something I can look at. In these assays it is usually H I S three. Or it is Lac Z. A colony in which Lac Z fires turns blue.”',
  ezcn:'<b>报告基因 ＝ 产物容易被看见的一个基因，放在待测的调控序列下游，于是「那段序列有没有被转录」变成我能看见的东西。</b><b>这些实验里通常是 HIS3 或 LacZ——LacZ 被打开的菌落会变蓝。</b>',
  mean:'他挑了一个零件问。<b>承重词</b>，前面几点里反复用到。',
  say:'“A reporter gene is a gene whose product is easy to see, placed downstream of the regulatory sequence being tested, so that transcription of that sequence becomes something I can look at. In these assays it is usually HIS3 or LacZ, and a colony in which LacZ fires turns blue.”'},

 {q:'What is a bait and what is a prey?',
  ez:'“The bait is the half that is known and fixed. It is the protein fused to the D N A binding domain. It sits on the regulatory region. That region is upstream of the reporter gene. The prey is the unknown half. Each insert of a complementary D N A library is fused to the activation domain. A prey that binds the bait switches the reporter on.”',
  ezcn:'<b>bait（诱饵）是已知、固定的那一半：融合在 DNA 结合结构域上的那个蛋白，坐在报告基因上游的调控区上。</b><b>prey（猎物）是未知的那一半：cDNA 文库的每一个插入片段都融合在激活结构域上；能结合 bait 的 prey 就把报告基因打开。</b>',
  mean:'术语。答得干脆说明你不是在背比喻。',
  say:'“The bait is the half that is known and fixed. It is the protein fused to the DNA binding domain, and it sits on the regulatory region upstream of the reporter gene. The prey is the unknown half. Each insert of a complementary DNA library is fused to the activation domain, and a prey that binds the bait switches the reporter on.”'},

 {q:'Why is a tag used instead of an antibody against the protein itself?',
  ez:'“Because raising a specific antibody is slow and expensive. For an uncharacterised protein there may be none at all. A tag is a short peptide. A ready made antibody already recognises it. So the same two antibodies work for any pair of proteins I test.”',
  ezcn:'因为<b>给一个新蛋白做特异性抗体又慢又贵，而且对未表征的蛋白可能根本没有</b>。<b>标签是一小段肽，现成的商品抗体就认得它——所以同样两个抗体可以用在我想测的任何一对蛋白上。</b><b>（pe-pur 那张卡上的标签是为了纯化，这里是为了沉淀：同一段多肽，两个用途。）</b>',
  mean:'实操层的问题。答得出来说明你想过成本。',
  say:'“Raising a specific antibody against a new protein is slow and expensive, and for an uncharacterised protein there may be none. A tag is a short peptide that a ready made antibody already recognises, so the same two antibodies work for any pair of proteins I want to test.”',
  tail:'<b>接卡 pe-pur</b>：那张卡上的标签是为了纯化，这里是为了沉淀。同一段多肽，两个用途。'},

 {q:'Your co-immunoprecipitation is positive. Is the interaction direct?',
  ez:'“Not necessarily. A co precipitation puts two proteins in one pelleted complex. They may touch each other. Or a third thing in the lysate may hold both. The gel does not separate those two cases. To answer it I would repeat the pull down. I would use two purified recombinant proteins. Then there is no third partner in the tube.”',
  ezcn:'<b>不一定。</b><b>共沉淀说明的是两个蛋白在同一个被沉下来的复合物里；它们是彼此接触，还是各自被裂解液里的第三个东西拉着——胶分不开这两种情况。</b><b>要回答它，我会用两个纯化的重组蛋白重做 pull-down，管子里就没有第三者了。</b>⚠ <b>答 yes 就输了；答 not necessarily 再说怎么验证，是满分。</b>',
  mean:'⚠ <b>这是这张卡上最锋利的一刀</b>，专门抓「把复合物说成接触」。',
  say:'“Not necessarily. A co-precipitation puts the two proteins in one pelleted complex. Whether they touch each other, or are both held by a third thing in the lysate, is a question the gel does not separate. To answer it I would repeat the pull-down with two purified recombinant proteins, so there is no third partner in the tube.”',
  tail:'答 “yes” 就输了。<b>答 “not necessarily” 再给出怎么验证，是满分。</b>'},

 {q:'You see no FRET signal. Do the two proteins interact?',
  ez:'“I cannot conclude that they do not. Energy transfer needs three conditions at once. Any one of them failing gives no signal. They may bind with the fluorophores badly oriented. Or the fluorophores may be too far apart. I would move the tag to the other terminus. Then I would repeat the experiment.”',
  ezcn:'<b>我不能由此断定它们不结合。</b><b>能量转移要三个条件同时成立，任何一个不成立都是「无信号」：它们可能结合了，但两个荧光基团取向不合适，或者离得太远。</b><b>我会把标签从一端挪到另一端再做一次。</b><b>同样的道理：干扰之后表型很弱，也不能证明这个基因不重要——可能只是敲低不完全。</b>',
  mean:'⚠ <b>阴性结果的解释</b>，最能分出「做过」和「背过」。',
  say:'“I cannot conclude that they do not. Energy transfer needs three conditions at once, and any one of them failing gives no signal. They may bind with the two fluorophores in an unsuitable orientation, or too far apart. I would move the tag from one terminus to the other and repeat it.”'},

 {q:'What is the difference between a knockout and a knockdown?',
  ez:'“A knockout removes the gene from the chromosome. So the product is absent. A knockdown leaves the gene in the genome. It destroys the message instead. So the product is reduced. Interference gives a knockdown. The phenotype it produces is a reduction. It is not an absence.”',
  ezcn:'<b>knockout（敲除）是把基因从染色体上拿掉，产物「没有」；knockdown（敲低）把基因留在基因组里、毁掉它的 mRNA，产物「变少」。</b><b>RNA 干扰给的是敲低，它造成的表型是「减少」而不是「缺失」。</b>',
  mean:'两个常被说反的词。他可能顺着 RNAi 问过来。',
  say:'“A knockout removes the gene from the chromosome, so the product is absent. A knockdown leaves the gene in the genome and destroys its message, so the product is reduced. Interference gives a knockdown, and the phenotype it produces is a reduction rather than an absence.”',
  tail:'<b>加一句更稳</b>：“That also means a weak phenotype after interference does not prove the gene is unimportant. It may just mean the knockdown was incomplete.”'},

 {q:'Why did you choose that method rather than another?',
  ez:'“I chose it because of what I needed the readout to be. I needed a number rather than a yes. A qualitative precipitation would not have answered my question. There is a trade off. The bait is on a chip and not in a cell. So I am measuring the binding. I am not measuring the biology.”',
  ezcn:'<b>我选它，是因为我需要的读出是什么。</b><b>我要的是一个数，不是一个「是」——定性的沉淀回答不了我的问题。</b><b>代价是：诱饵在芯片上，不在细胞里，所以我测到的是结合，不是生物学。</b><b>「我选它是因为我要的读出是什么」这个形状可以套到任何方法上。</b>',
  mean:'他其实在问<b>你有没有想过替代方案</b>。答一个理由不够，要答一个<b>取舍</b>。',
  say:'“I chose it because of what I needed the readout to be. I needed a number rather than a yes, so a qualitative precipitation would not have answered my question. The trade-off is that the bait is on a chip and not in a cell, so I am measuring the binding and not the biology.”',
  tail:'<b>「我选它是因为我要的读出是什么」这个形状可以套到任何方法上。</b>'},

 {q:'Why does a pull-down need a tube with nothing added to it?',
  ez:'“Because the signal on its own means nothing. In a pull down the control tube holds the bare tag. It has the same beads and the same lysate. A band is informative only under one condition. It must be present with the fusion. And it must be absent with the bare tag. The control tube is what makes the gel readable at all.”',
  ezcn:'因为<b>信号本身什么都不说明</b>。<b>pull-down 里那一管对照放的是光秃秃的标签，珠子一样、裂解液一样。</b><b>一条带有意义只有一个条件：在融合蛋白那管里有、在光标签那管里没有。</b><b>那管对照才是让这张胶读得出来的东西。</b>',
  mean:'听起来像最基础的问题，其实问的是<b>对照在逻辑上干什么</b>。',
  say:'“Because the signal on its own means nothing. In a pull-down the control tube has the bare tag with the same beads and the same lysate, and a band is only informative if it is present with the fusion and absent with the bare tag. The control tube is what makes the gel readable at all.”',
  odd:1},

 {q:'Why can a microscope not show two proteins bound together?',
  ez:'“Because a contact is one to ten nanometres. A light microscope cannot resolve that distance. So every method here reports a downstream signal instead. Energy transfer comes closest of all of them. And even that reports a change of emitted wavelength. It does not give an image.”',
  ezcn:'因为<b>「接触」这件事的尺度是 1–10 纳米，光学显微镜分辨不了</b>。<b>所以这里每一个方法报的都是一个下游信号。</b><b>能量转移是最接近的一个，可就连它报的也是发射波长的改变，而不是一张图像。</b>',
  mean:'他在问<b>分辨率</b>，而这正好是这张卡的第一句。',
  say:'“Because the distance that defines a contact is one to ten nanometres, and a light microscope cannot resolve that. That is why every method here reports a downstream signal instead. Energy transfer is the closest any of them gets, and even that reports a change of emitted wavelength rather than an image.”',
  odd:1},

 {q:'How can a bacterial toxin stand in for a plant hormone?',
  ez:'“Coronatine is a bacterial toxin. It resembles methyl jasmonate in structure. It resembles it in function too. In the resonance experiment it drove the same protein pair. It reached about three hundred and ten units. That is close to what the plant molecule gave. So the receptor is responding to a shape. A molecule from another organism with that shape works.”',
  ezcn:'<b>冠菌素（coronatine）是一个细菌毒素，在结构和功能上都像茉莉酸甲酯。</b><b>在那个共振实验里，它把同一对蛋白推到约 310 单位，跟植物自己那个分子给的数接近。</b><b>所以受体响应的是一个「形状」——另一个生物来的分子只要有这个形状就管用。</b>',
  mean:'他拿 SPR 那个实例的细节问机制。<b>答得出来说明你读懂了那张图而不只是记住了数字。</b>',
  say:'“Coronatine is a bacterial toxin that resembles methyl jasmonate in structure and in function. In the resonance experiment it drove the same protein pair to about three hundred and ten units, close to what the plant molecule gave. So the receptor is responding to a shape, and a molecule from another organism that has that shape works.”',
  odd:1},

 {q:'How can so little injected RNA switch off a whole gene?',
  ez:'“Because the product becomes the starting material again. An R N A dependent R N A polymerase copies the target message. It makes fresh double stranded R N A. That is cut into new small interfering R N A. And that re enters the cycle. So a low injected dose is amplified. The result is complete silencing.”',
  ezcn:'因为<b>产物又变回了原料</b>。<b>一个 RNA 依赖的 RNA 聚合酶把靶 mRNA 抄成新的双链 RNA，双链 RNA 又被切成新的 siRNA，再进入同一个循环。</b><b>所以注进去很小的量会被放大成完全的沉默。</b>',
  mean:'问的是<b>放大</b>。',
  say:'“Because the product becomes the starting material again. An RNA dependent RNA polymerase copies the target message into fresh double stranded RNA, that is cut into new small interfering RNA, and it re-enters the cycle. So a low injected dose is amplified into complete silencing.”',
  odd:1}
],

ask:[
 {g:'⚠ 考官 · Šulc · 质谱到底测什么', gn:'⚠ <b>2026-09-23 名单下来当天补的。</b><b>Doc. Miroslav Šulc 领生物分子结构功能蛋白质组学</b>，主力方法是<b>化学交联质谱（XL-MS）</b>：把非天然氨基酸掺进蛋白、光照交联、酶切、串联质谱定位。⚠ <b>量过：<code>proteomics</code> 在整套卡上 0 命中，<code>mass spectrometry</code> 只有 4 处</b>——而她的 <code>pe_cfps</code> 卡上非天然氨基酸有 15 处，<b>两边本来就该接上。</b><b>⚠ 他是方法论的严苛派，会问数据量够不够支撑结论。</b>', items:[
{r:'高', q:'What does a mass spectrometer actually measure?',
    ez:'“It measures a mass to charge ratio. It does not measure mass directly. The sample must be ionised first. Electrospray is one way and it makes multiply charged ions. M A L D I is the other common way. Then an analyser separates the ions by that ratio. A detector counts them. The charge state has to be worked out before a mass can be reported. That is why the spectrum shows an isotope pattern. The spacing of that pattern gives the charge.”',
    ezcn:'<b>它测的是<b>质荷比 m/z</b>，<b>不是质量本身</b>。</b><b>样品必须先<b>离子化</b>：<b>电喷雾（ESI）</b>会产生多电荷离子，<b>MALDI</b> 是另一种常用方式。</b><b>然后<b>质量分析器</b>按质荷比把离子分开，<b>检测器</b>数它们。</b>⚠ <b>要报出质量，必须先知道<b>电荷数</b>——而电荷数就是从谱图上那一组<b>同位素峰的间距</b>读出来的。</b>',
 en:'“It measures a mass-to-charge ratio, not mass directly. The sample has to be ionised first. Electrospray is one common way and it produces multiply charged ions, and MALDI is the other. An analyser then separates the ions by that ratio and a detector counts them. The charge state must be worked out before a mass can be reported, and that is what the isotope pattern is for, because the spacing of the isotope peaks gives the charge. This is general knowledge and not in the Czech textbook.”',
 cn:'⚠ <b>整条 general</b>：全书 0 命中。<br><br>⚠ <b>「测的是质荷比不是质量」这一句本身就是分数</b>，<b>因为它说明你没有把仪器当黑箱</b>——这正是 Hudeček 和 Šulc 两位共同的那条底线。'},
{r:'高', q:'How do you get from a spectrum to the name of a protein?',
    ez:'“The protein is cut into peptides first. Trypsin is the usual enzyme. It cuts after lysine and after arginine. So the peptide ends are known in advance. The peptides are then measured. One peptide can be selected and broken again. That second step is tandem mass spectrometry. The fragments differ by one residue at a time. So the series of differences reads out a sequence. That sequence is matched against a database. A false discovery rate has to be reported with the match.”',
    ezcn:'<b>先把蛋白<b>酶切成肽</b>，常用的酶是<b>胰蛋白酶</b>——<b>它在赖氨酸和精氨酸之后切</b>，所以<b>肽段的末端是事先就知道的</b>。</b><b>然后测这些肽；再<b>挑出一条肽把它打碎一次</b>，这第二步叫<b>串联质谱（MS/MS）</b>。</b>⚠ <b>碎片之间<b>每次差一个残基</b>，所以<b>这一串差值读出来就是序列</b>。</b><b>序列拿去跟数据库比对，<b>报结果必须同时报假发现率（FDR）</b>。</b>',
 en:'“The protein is cut into peptides first, usually with trypsin, which cuts after lysine and after arginine, so the peptide ends are known in advance. The peptides are measured, then one peptide is selected and broken again, and that second step is tandem mass spectrometry. The fragments differ by one residue at a time, so the series of mass differences reads out a sequence, and that sequence is matched against a database. A false discovery rate has to be reported with the match, because a database search will always return something. This is general knowledge.”',
 cn:'⚠ <b>整条 general</b>。<b>最后那半句是专门为他准备的</b>：<b>数据库检索永远会给你一个结果，所以报匹配就必须报 FDR</b>。<b>他记录在案的提问方式是问「实验数量够不够支撑结论」</b>——<b>主动说出 FDR 和序列覆盖率，就是先把这一刀接住。</b><br><br><b>接口</b>：胰蛋白酶切在赖／精之后，这跟卡 <b>aa</b> 讲的<b>带正电的那两个氨基酸</b>是同一件事；Western blot 和免疫共沉淀在这张卡上已有，<b>质谱是它们的下一步</b>。'},
{r:'中', q:'What does cross-linking add that you cannot get otherwise?',
    ez:'“It adds distance. A cross linker is a molecule with two reactive ends. The spacer between them has a known length. If it joins two residues those residues were close enough. So each cross link is an upper limit on a distance. Many such limits together give the architecture of a complex. This works on complexes that will not crystallise. It also works on interactions that are short lived. A zero length linker joins a carboxyl group straight to an amine.”',
    ezcn:'<b>它加的是<b>距离</b>。</b><b>交联剂是一个<b>两端都能反应</b>的分子，中间那段<b>间隔臂的长度是已知的</b>。</b>⚠ <b>所以如果它把两个残基连上了，就说明<b>这两个残基当时离得足够近</b>——<b>每一条交联就是一个「距离上限」</b>；很多个上限拼在一起，就得到复合物的<b>架构</b>。</b><b>这套方法对<b>长不出晶体</b>的复合物和<b>瞬时的相互作用</b>都管用。</b><b>零长度交联剂则是把一个<b>羧基直接接到一个氨基</b>上。</b>',
 en:'“It adds distance. A cross-linker is a molecule with two reactive ends and a spacer of known length between them. If it joins two residues, those residues were close enough to be joined, so each cross-link is an upper limit on a distance. Many such limits together give the architecture of a complex. This works on complexes that will not crystallise and on interactions that are short lived. A zero-length linker joins a carboxyl group straight to an amine with no spacer at all. This is general knowledge.”',
 cn:'⚠ <b>整条 general</b>。<b>这是 Šulc 整个实验室的那句话</b>：<b>交联质谱给的不是结构，是一组距离约束</b>——<b>说清楚这个区别本身就是加分</b>。<br><br>⚠ <b>跟她自己的卡接得上</b>：<code>pe_cfps</code> 上的<b>非天然氨基酸</b>（15 处）正是他把光敏基团装进蛋白的办法 —— <b>掺进去、用紫外照一下，交联就在原位发生</b>。<b>如果他问到无细胞体系或者密码子扩展，那条路她本来就熟。</b>'},
  {r:'高', q:'What is a dalton, exactly?',
    ez:'“A dalton is the unit for atomic and molecular mass. It is defined as one twelfth of the mass of a carbon twelve atom. That is about one point six six times ten to the minus twenty seven kilograms. It is close to the mass of one proton. So a fifty kilodalton protein has fifty thousand times that mass.”',
    ezcn:'<b>道尔顿是原子和分子质量的单位</b>，<b>定义为碳-12 原子质量的十二分之一</b>，<b>约 1.66 乘十的负二十七次方千克</b>，<b>接近一个质子的质量</b>。<b>所以一个 50 千道尔顿的蛋白，质量是它的五万倍。</b>',
   en:'“A dalton is the unit used for atomic and molecular mass. It is defined as one twelfth of the mass of a carbon-12 atom. That is about 1.66 times ten to the minus twenty-seven kilograms. It is close to the mass of a single proton. So a fifty-kilodalton protein has fifty thousand times that mass.”',
   cn:'<b>定义要给「十二分之一的碳-12」，不要只说「原子质量单位」</b> —— 后者是同义反复。<span class="pg">通用</span>'},
  {r:'高', q:'Why does one pure peptide give a cluster of peaks rather than a single peak?',
    ez:'“Because of isotopes. Isotopes are atoms of one element with different numbers of neutrons. In nature about one point one percent of carbon is carbon thirteen. A peptide has many carbons. So some molecules carry one carbon thirteen. Some carry two. Each extra neutron adds about one dalton. The spectrum therefore shows a series of peaks about one apart.”',
    ezcn:'<b>因为同位素。</b><b>同位素是质子数相同、中子数不同的同种元素。</b><b>自然界的碳约有百分之一点一是碳-13。</b><b>一个肽段有很多碳，所以总有一部分分子带一个碳-13，一部分带两个。</b><b>每多一个中子就多约一道尔顿，所以谱上是一串间隔约一的峰。</b>',
   en:'“Because of isotopes, which are atoms of the same element with different numbers of neutrons. About one point one percent of natural carbon is carbon-13, and a peptide has many carbons, so some molecules carry one carbon-13 and some carry two. Each extra neutron adds roughly one dalton, so the spectrum shows a series of peaks about one apart rather than a single sharp peak.”',
   cn:'<b>他问这个是在查你知不知道谱图上那一簇是什么。</b>说出百分之一点一这个数，比只说「因为同位素」有分量。<span class="pg">通用</span>'},
  {r:'高', q:'Why must native mass spectrometry use ammonium acetate rather than PBS?',
    ez:'“Because the buffer has to leave. Native mass spectrometry keeps the complex folded on its way into the gas phase. Ammonium acetate is volatile. It evaporates off the ion completely. Phosphate buffered saline is not volatile. Sodium, potassium and phosphate stay on the surface. They form many salt adducts. The peaks broaden and the real mass is buried.”',
    ezcn:'<b>因为缓冲盐必须能走掉。</b><b>非变性质谱要让复合体保持折叠状态进气相。</b><b>醋酸铵是挥发性的，能从离子上完全挥发掉。</b><b>磷酸缓冲盐不挥发：钠、钾、磷酸根留在表面，形成大量盐加合物，峰被展宽，真实质量就被埋掉了。</b>',
   en:'“Because the buffer has to leave. Native mass spectrometry keeps the complex folded on its way into the gas phase. Ammonium acetate is volatile and evaporates off the ion completely. Phosphate-buffered saline is not volatile, so sodium, potassium and phosphate stay on the surface and form many salt adducts. The peaks broaden and the real mass is buried.”',
   cn:'<b>判据一句：缓冲盐挥发不掉，就挂在离子上。</b>⚠ 卡 <b>pe-pur</b> 上也有「醋酸铵」，那是<b>离子交换的洗脱液</b>，两回事。<span class="pg">通用</span>'},
  {r:'高', q:'Why can complete-mass spectrometry not tell leucine from isoleucine?',
    ez:'“Because they are isomers. Same formula, same exact mass. No resolution helps. To separate them you have to break the side chain, not just the peptide bond. High energy fragmentation gives side chain specific ions, the d and w types. Those differ because the branch sits in a different place. So you need tandem mass spectrometry with high energy dissociation.”',
    ezcn:'<b>因为它们是同分异构体：分子式相同、精确质量也相同，分辨率再高也没用。</b><b>要分开它们，必须打断侧链本身，而不只是打断肽键。</b><b>高能碎裂能给出侧链特异的碎片离子（d 型和 w 型），它们因为支链位置不同而有差别。</b><b>所以要用带高能解离的串联质谱。</b>',
   en:'“Because they are isomers: same formula and same exact mass, so no amount of resolution separates them. To tell them apart you have to break the side chain rather than only the peptide bond. High-energy fragmentation gives side-chain-specific ions, the d and w types, which differ because the branch sits in a different position. So it needs tandem mass spectrometry with high-energy dissociation.”',
   cn:'<b>「分辨率再高也没用」这半句一定要说</b>，那才说明你懂为什么 —— 不是仪器不够好，是质量真的一样。<span class="pg">通用</span>'},
  {r:'中', q:'EDC is called a zero-length crosslinker. Which two side-chain groups does it join?',
    ez:'“It joins a carboxyl to a primary amine. E D C itself is not the bridge. It activates the carboxyl group first. That carboxyl is on aspartate, on glutamate, or at the C terminus. The activated intermediate then reacts with a nearby primary amine. That amine is on lysine or at the N terminus. The bond formed is an amide. No spacer is added at all. So the two residues must already be very close.”',
    ezcn:'<b>它把一个羧基连到一个伯胺上。</b><b>EDC 本身不是那座桥：它先活化羧基</b>（天冬氨酸、谷氨酸侧链，或者 C 端），<b>活化中间体再跟附近的伯胺反应</b>（赖氨酸侧链，或者 N 端），<b>形成酰胺键，完全不引入间隔臂。</b><b>所以被连上的两个残基本来就必须很近。</b>',
   en:'“It joins a carboxyl group to a primary amine. EDC itself is not the bridge: it activates the carboxyl first, on aspartate, glutamate or the C-terminus, and the activated intermediate then reacts with a nearby primary amine on lysine or the N-terminus. The bond formed is an amide and no spacer is added at all, so the two residues must already be very close.”',
   cn:'<b>零长度这个词就是答案的一半</b>：没有间隔臂，所以一个交联点是一条<b>很短</b>的距离约束。接这张卡的交联质谱那一格。<span class="pg">通用</span>'},
  {r:'中', q:'Why does crosslinking mass spectrometry blow up the search space?',
    ez:'“Because you are matching two peptides at once. In normal proteomics one spectrum is matched to one peptide from the database. The space grows with the number of peptides. In crosslinking, any peptide can in principle be linked to any other. So the candidate count goes as the number of peptides squared. That is the N squared problem. It is quadratic, not exponential. The fixes are to enrich the crosslinked peptides and to limit the database to proteins you already believe interact.”',
    ezcn:'<b>因为你一次要匹配两条肽段。</b><b>普通蛋白质组学是一张谱对一条肽段，搜索空间随肽段数增长。</b><b>交联质谱里任意两条肽段原则上都可能连在一起，所以候选组合数是肽段数的平方 —— 就是 N 平方问题。</b>⚠ <b>是平方级，不是指数级。</b><b>对策是富集交联肽段，以及把数据库限制在已经相信有互作的蛋白上。</b>',
   en:'“Because you are matching two peptides at once. In normal proteomics one spectrum is matched to one peptide from the database, and the space grows with the number of peptides. In crosslinking, any peptide can in principle be linked to any other, so the number of candidates goes as the number of peptides squared. That is the N-squared problem. It is quadratic, not exponential. The usual fixes are to enrich the crosslinked peptides and to limit the database to proteins you already believe interact.”',
   cn:'⚠ <b>「平方级，不是指数级」这半句要主动说</b>。她 2026-09-25 那份准备材料的题面写的是「指数级增长」，那是用词错了 —— 对着方法论严苛派说错这个词很吃亏。<span class="pg">通用</span>'},
]},

 {g:'术语表 · 这张卡上剩下的名字', gn:'方法本身在上面的「方法速查」里，顺式元件、最简启动子、转录激活域、标签、Dicer、RISC 在下面的「定义类」里。<b>这一组只收两边都没收的那几个名字。</b>形式一样：<b>名字 ＝ 是什么 · 管什么 · 读出来是什么</b>。', items:[
  {r:'高', q:'bait and prey',
   ez:'“The bait is the half you already know. It is fused to the D N A binding domain. The prey is the half you are testing. It is fused to the activation domain. The two halves may bind. Then the domains are brought together and the reporter gene fires.”',
   ezcn:'<b>诱饵（bait）＝ 已知的那一半，融合在 DNA 结合域上，固定不动。</b><b>猎物（prey）＝ 要测的那一半，融合在转录激活域上（常常来自一个文库）。</b>⚠ <b>两半一结合，两个结构域就被牽到一起，报告基因点着。</b>',
   en:'“The bait is the half you already know, fused to the DNA-binding domain. The prey is the half you are testing, fused to the activation domain and often drawn from a library. If bait and prey bind, the two domains are brought together and the reporter gene fires.”'},
  {r:'高', q:'DNA-binding domain',
   ez:'“A D N A binding domain is the part of a factor that recognises a sequence. Its own sequence decides which promoter or enhancer it binds. It carries no activating power of its own. In a two hybrid assay it is the anchor. It holds the bait over the reporter promoter.”',
   ezcn:'<b>DNA 结合域 ＝ 因子身上负责「认序列」的那一块；它自己的序列决定了它认哪个启动子或哪个增强子。</b>⚠ <b>它自己不带激活能力——在双杂交里它就是一个锚，把诱饵固定在报告基因的启动子上方。</b>',
   en:'“A DNA-binding domain is the part of a transcription factor that recognises a sequence, and its own sequence decides which promoter or enhancer it binds. It carries no activating power of its own. In a two-hybrid assay it is the anchor holding the bait over the reporter promoter.”'},
  {r:'高', q:'fusion protein',
   ez:'“A fusion protein is one protein made from two coding sequences joined together. The cell translates them as a single chain. So the two parts are physically tied. Every hybrid method on this card depends on that. It lets you put a known domain onto an unknown protein.”',
   ezcn:'<b>融合蛋白 ＝ 把两段编码序列接在一起、翻译成的单条链。</b>⚠ <b>两部分因此在物理上被拴在一起——这张卡上所有「杂交」方法都建立在这一点上：把一个已知的结构域装到一个未知蛋白身上。</b>',
   en:'“A fusion protein is a single chain translated from two coding sequences joined together, so the two parts are physically tied. Every hybrid method on this card depends on that, because it lets you put a known domain onto an unknown protein.”'},
  {r:'高', q:'GST and the glutathione bead',
   ez:'“G S T is glutathione S transferase. It is used as a tag on the bait protein. It has affinity for glutathione. The glutathione is coupled to agarose beads. So the tagged bait sticks to the beads. Spinning the beads down brings the bait and whatever bound it.”',
   ezcn:'<b>GST ＝ 谷胱甘肽 S-转移酶，当标签用。</b><b>它对偶联在琼脂糖球珠上的谷胱甘肽有亲和性，所以带 GST 的诱饵会黏在球珠上。</b><b>离心把球珠沉下来，诱饵和挂在它身上的东西一起下来。</b>',
   en:'“GST is glutathione S-transferase, used as a tag on the bait protein. It has affinity for glutathione coupled to agarose beads, so the tagged bait sticks to them, and spinning the beads down brings the bait and whatever bound it.”'},
  {r:'高', q:'CFP and YFP',
   ez:'“C F P is cyan fluorescent protein. Y F P is yellow fluorescent protein. One is put on each of the two proteins being tested. Their spectra overlap. That is one of the three conditions for energy transfer. If the two proteins come close the energy passes across. The readout is a change in the emitted wavelength.”',
   ezcn:'<b>CFP ＝ 青荧光蛋白；YFP ＝ 黄荧光蛋白。</b><b>两个待测蛋白上各接一个；它们的光谱重叠，而重叠正是能量转移的三个条件之一。</b><b>两个蛋白一靠近，能量就传过去，读出的是发射波长的变化。</b>',
   en:'“CFP is cyan fluorescent protein and YFP is yellow fluorescent protein. One is put on each of the two proteins being tested, and their overlapping spectra are one of the three conditions for energy transfer. If the proteins come close the energy passes across, and the readout is a change in the emitted wavelength.”'},
  {r:'高', q:'coronatine and methyl jasmonate',
   ez:'“Methyl jasmonate is a plant hormone. Coronatine is a toxin made by bacteria. It resembles methyl jasmonate in structure and in what it does. So it can stand in for the hormone in an experiment. In the resonance experiment it drove the same protein pair.”',
   ezcn:'<b>茉莉酸甲酯 ＝ 一种植物激素；冠菌素（coronatine）＝ 细菌造的一种毒素。</b>⚠ <b>冠菌素在结构和功能上都像茉莉酸甲酯，所以实验里可以拿它代替激素——共振实验里它驱动的是同一对蛋白。</b>',
   en:'“Methyl jasmonate is a plant hormone and coronatine is a toxin made by bacteria. Coronatine resembles methyl jasmonate in structure and in function, so it can stand in for the hormone in an experiment, and in the resonance experiment it drove the same protein pair.”'},
  {r:'高', q:'dsRNA and RdRP',
   ez:'“A double stranded R N A is R N A with two paired strands. It is what triggers interference. R d R P is R N A dependent R N A polymerase. It makes R N A using R N A as the template. It amplifies the small interfering R N As, so a weak signal spreads. Plants and worms and yeast have it.”',
   ezcn:'<b>双链 RNA（dsRNA）＝ 两条配对的 RNA，它就是触发干扰的那个东西。</b><b>RdRP ＝ RNA 依赖的 RNA 聚合酶，以 RNA 为模板合成 RNA。</b>⚠ <b>它把 siRNA 扩增出次级 siRNA，于是一个弱信号被放大。植物、线虫、酵母有这套，哺乳动物和果蝇没找到。</b>',
   en:'“A double-stranded RNA is RNA with two paired strands, and it is what triggers interference. RdRP is RNA-dependent RNA polymerase, which makes RNA using RNA as the template. It amplifies the interfering RNAs into secondary ones, so a weak signal spreads. Plants, nematodes and yeast have it, while mammals and Drosophila do not.”'},
  {r:'高', q:'solid matrix and antibody in a precipitation',
   ez:'“A solid matrix is something the experiment can spin down. Beads or a membrane are the usual ones. An antibody that recognises the target is attached to it. The mixture is added and whatever binds the target comes down too. So the readout is what is in the pellet.”',
   ezcn:'<b>固体基质 ＝ 实验里能被沉下来的那个东西（球珠或微膜）。</b><b>把认靶蛋白的抗体接在上面，加入混合物，凡是结合靶蛋白的就跟着一起沉下来。</b>⚠ <b>所以读出就是「沉淀里有什么」。</b>',
   en:'“A solid matrix is something the experiment can bring down, usually beads or a membrane. An antibody recognising the target is attached to it, the mixture is added, and whatever binds the target comes down too. So the readout is what is in the pellet.”'},
 ]},

 {g:'方法速查 · 这几张卡上出现的实验，各自在测什么', gn:'⚠ <b>2026-09-21 她说：「方法学我不先了解一下直接看卡我完全看不懂」。</b>查下来她是对的：下面这几个方法在四张分子生物学卡上被点名用到，<b>全套材料里却没有一句解释</b>。每一条只回答三件事：<b>它是什么 · 它测的是什么 · 读出来的是什么</b>。', items:[
  {r:'高', q:'What is a Southern blot, and what is a Northern blot?',
   ez:'“A Southern blot and a Northern blot are the same procedure on different material. Both separate nucleic acid by size on a gel. Both then transfer it onto a membrane. Both then find one sequence with a labelled probe. The probe finds its target by base pairing. Southern blotting is done on D N A. Northern blotting is done on R N A. So a Southern blot answers one question. Is this sequence present in the genome. A Northern blot answers a different one. Is this gene being transcribed.”',
   ezcn:'<b>两者是同一套动作：先用凝胶电泳按大小分开核酸，再转印到膜上，再用一条带标记的探针靠碱基配对把某一条序列找出来。</b>⚠ <b>差别只在膜上的是什么：Southern 印迹做的是 DNA，Northern 印迹做的是 RNA。</b><b>所以 Southern 回答「基因组里还在不在」，Northern 回答「这个基因正在不正在被转录」。</b>',
   en:'“A Southern blot and a Northern blot are the same set of moves carried out on different material. Nucleic acid is separated by size on a gel, transferred onto a membrane, and one particular sequence is then found with a labelled probe that binds it by base pairing. The only difference is what is on the membrane. A Southern blot is done on DNA and a Northern blot on RNA. So they answer different questions. A Southern blot asks whether a sequence is still present in the genome, which is how a knockout is confirmed. A Northern blot asks whether that gene is being transcribed, and it also shows the size of the transcript. A Western blot is the same idea again with protein on the membrane and an antibody as the probe.”'},
  {r:'高', q:'What is in situ hybridisation?',
   ez:'“It is hybridisation done inside the cell or tissue. A labelled probe binds its target by base pairing. The target stays where it is. So the readout is a picture and not a band. It tells you where a sequence sits. It also tells you how much is there. That is what a blot cannot do. A blot needs the material ground up first.”',
   ezcn:'<b>原位杂交 ＝ 把杂交这件事放在细胞或组织里做：带标记的探针靠碱基配对找到靶序列，而靶序列一直呆在它原来的位置上。</b>⚠ <b>所以读出来的是一张图，不是一条带</b>——它告诉你这条序列<b>在哪里</b>、有<b>多少</b>。<b>而印迹做不到这一点，因为印迹要先把材料砸碎。</b>',
   en:'“In situ hybridisation is hybridisation carried out inside the cell or tissue rather than on a membrane. A labelled probe finds its target sequence by base pairing while the target stays exactly where it was, so the readout is an image rather than a band. It tells you where in the specimen a sequence is and roughly how much of it there is. A blot cannot do that, because a blot requires the material to be ground up first, which destroys the spatial information. The nematode RNA interference experiment used it that way, to ask what the level of the endogenous message was in the embryos.”'},
  {r:'高', q:'What is microinjection?',
   ez:'“It is putting material straight into one cell with a fine needle. D N A or R N A or protein can go in. The point is that the dose is known. The place is known too. And the cell is a particular cell you chose. So the experiment has no delivery step to argue about. That is why it was used to settle the R N A interference question.”',
   ezcn:'<b>显微注射 ＝ 用一根很细的针把材料直接送进一个细胞里（DNA、RNA、蛋白都行）。</b>⚠ <b>它的价值在于三件事都是确定的：剂量确定、位置确定、进的是你选定的那个细胞</b>——于是“东西没进去”这个可能性被排除了。<b>1998 年线虫那个实验就是这样定下 RNAi 的。</b>',
   en:'“Microinjection is putting material directly into a single cell through a very fine needle, and DNA, RNA or protein can all go in that way. Its value is that three things are known at once: the dose, the place, and which particular cell received it. That removes any argument about whether the material got in, which is why it settled the RNA interference question. Antisense RNA and double-stranded RNA against the same gene were injected into nematode gonad cells side by side, and only the double-stranded one silenced the endogenous message.”'},
  {r:'高', q:'What is a reporter gene?',
   ez:'“A reporter gene is a gene whose product is easy to see. lacZ and G U S and the fluorescent proteins are the usual ones. You put it under the control you want to study. Then its signal stands in for that control. So you read colour or light instead of reading the real product. The real product may be hard to measure. Or it may not exist yet in that cell.”',
   ezcn:'<b>报告基因 ＝ 产物容易被看见的基因</b>（常用 lacZ、GUS、荧光蛋白）。<b>把它放在你要研究的那个控制之下，它的信号就替代那个控制被读出来</b>——你看的是颜色或荧光，而不是真正的产物。⚠ <b>因为真正的产物可能很难测，也可能在那个细胞里根本还不存在。</b>',
   en:'“A reporter gene is a gene whose product is easy to detect, and lacZ, GUS and the fluorescent proteins are the usual choices. You place it under the control you want to study, and its signal then stands in for that control, so you read colour or light instead of the real product. That matters because the real product may be hard to measure, or may not exist in the cell at all. It is used that way throughout these cards. In the yeast two-hybrid system the reporter is switched on only when two proteins meet. In gene trapping a promoterless reporter lights up only where it has interrupted an active gene. And a reporter with a weak basal promoter reports whether an enhancer is nearby.”'},
  {r:'高', q:'What is an EMSA or gel shift assay?',
   ez:'“It asks whether a protein binds a particular piece of D N A. A labelled D N A fragment is run on a gel. It is run once alone and once with the protein. Free D N A runs fast. D N A with a protein on it runs slower. So a shifted band means something bound. Add an antibody and the band shifts further. That second shift names which protein it was.”',
   ezcn:'<b>凝胶阵移实验（EMSA，又叫 gel shift）问的是：某个蛋白会不会结合某一段 DNA。</b><b>把带标记的 DNA 片段在胶上跑两次：一次单独跑，一次和蛋白一起跑。</b>⚠ <b>游离的 DNA 跑得快，身上挂了蛋白的跑得慢——带往上“移”了，就说明有东西结合上去了。</b><b>再加一支抗体，带会再移一次，那一次才告诉你结合的到底是哪个蛋白。</b>',
   en:'“An electrophoretic mobility shift assay, also called a gel shift, asks whether a protein binds a particular piece of DNA. A labelled DNA fragment is run on a gel twice, once on its own and once after incubation with the protein. Free DNA runs fast, and DNA with a protein bound to it runs more slowly, so a shifted band means something bound. Adding an antibody against a candidate protein shifts the band further still, and that second shift, the supershift, is what names which protein it was. It is the in vitro counterpart of the chromatin immunoprecipitation on this card, which asks the same question inside a living cell.”'},
  {r:'高', q:'What is density gradient centrifugation, and what is a polysome profile?',
   ez:'“A tube is filled with a gradient of increasing density. The sample is layered on top and spun. Each particle settles where the density matches its own. So particles are separated by how heavy they are. Ribosomes work well on such a gradient. A message being translated carries many ribosomes. It is heavy and sinks far. A message not being translated carries none. So the profile shows which messages are being read.”',
   ezcn:'<b>密度梯度离心 ＝ 管子里装一个从上到下密度递增的梯度，样品铺在最上面，离心之后每一种颗粒停在密度与它相等的那一层</b>——按“有多重”把东西分开。⚠ <b>用在核糖体上就是多核糖体分析：一条正在被翻译的 mRNA 身上挂着好多核糖体，很重、沉得深；没在被翻译的一个也不挂。</b><b>所以这张图读的是“哪些 mRNA 正在被读”——mb-post 上 miRNA 压翻译的那个实验用的就是它。</b>',
   en:'“A tube is filled with a gradient of increasing density, the sample is layered on top and the tube is spun, and each kind of particle settles at the level where the density matches its own. So the method separates things by how heavy they are. Applied to ribosomes it becomes polysome profiling. A message that is being translated carries many ribosomes, so it is heavy and sinks far down the gradient, while a message that is not being translated carries none and stays near the top. The profile therefore reads out which messages are actually being read. That is the experiment behind the micro RNA result on the card about layers beyond transcription: with the micro RNA present the target message moved out of the polysomes and free ribosomes increased.”'},

  {r:'高', q:'What is a yeast one-hybrid assay?',
   ez:'“A yeast one hybrid assay asks which protein binds a known piece of D N A. It runs inside a living yeast cell. The known element is cloned upstream of a minimal promoter. A minimal promoter is stripped back to its core. It is too weak to fire by itself. A reporter gene is joined downstream of that promoter. The candidate protein is made as a fusion. Its partner in the fusion is a transcription activation domain. A protein that binds the element drags that domain over. The promoter then fires and the reporter is transcribed. So binding to D N A is read out as a blue colony.”',
   ezcn:'<b>酵母单杂交 ＝ 问「哪个蛋白结合这段已知 DNA」，在活的酵母细胞里做。</b><b>把已知顺式元件克隆到最小启动子 Pmin 上游（Pmin ＝ 剥到只剩核心的启动子，自己弱到点不着火），报告基因接在 Pmin 下游；待测蛋白与酵母转录激活域做成融合蛋白。</b>⚠ <b>蛋白一结合到元件上，就把激活域拽到 Pmin，Pmin 点火，报告基因被转录——于是「结合 DNA」被读成了「蓝色菌落」。完整版在速背 04。</b>',
   en:'“A yeast one-hybrid assay identifies a protein that binds stably to a known piece of DNA, and it works inside a living yeast cell. The known cis-acting element is cloned upstream of a minimal promoter called Pmin, and a reporter gene is joined downstream of it. The candidate protein is expressed as a fusion with a yeast transcription activation domain. A protein that binds the element drags its attached activation domain to Pmin, Pmin fires, and the reporter gene is transcribed. So binding to a piece of DNA is read out as expression of a reporter. The full version is on this card under the cramming points.”'},
  {r:'高', q:'What is a yeast two-hybrid assay?',
   ez:'“A yeast two hybrid assay asks whether two proteins bind each other. It uses the same parts as the one hybrid. But the D N A binding half is now a protein as well. The known protein is fused to a D N A binding domain. That fusion is the bait. The unknown protein is fused to an activation domain. That fusion is the prey. Bait and prey may bind. Then the two domains are brought together. The reporter gene is then transcribed.”',
   ezcn:'<b>酵母双杂交 ＝ 问「这两个蛋白会不会结合」，用的是跟单杂交同一套零件。</b><b>已知蛋白融合到 DNA 结合域上，叫诱饵（bait）；未知蛋白融合到转录激活域上，叫猎物（prey）。</b>⚠ <b>两者一结合，两个结构域就被牽到一起，报告基因被转录——这整套能成立，是因为转录调控因子是组件式的（速背 06）。完整版在速背 07。</b>',
   en:'“A yeast two-hybrid assay asks whether two proteins bind each other, and it uses the same parts as the one-hybrid with one change: the half that recognises the DNA is now a protein too. The known protein is fused to a DNA-binding domain and that fusion is the bait. The candidate is fused to a transcription activation domain and that fusion is the prey. If bait and prey bind, the two domains are brought together over the reporter promoter and the reporter gene is transcribed. The whole thing works only because a transcription factor is modular, with its DNA-binding and activation domains separable.”'},
  {r:'高', q:'What is surface plasmon resonance?',
   ez:'“Surface plasmon resonance measures binding on a chip without any label. The bait protein is immobilised on a dextran layer. That layer sits on a metal film a few nanometres thick. A protein mixture is flowed past it. Anything that binds raises the refractive index at the surface. That shifts the resonance angle. The resonance angle is where reflected light loses intensity. The shift is proportional to how much bound. So the readout is a quantity and not a yes.”',
   ezcn:'<b>表面等离子体共振（SPR）＝ 在芯片上、不用任何标记测结合。</b><b>诱饵蛋白固定在葡聚糖层上，那层贴在纳米级的金属膜表面；蛋白混合物流过，凡是结合上去的就抬高膜表面的折射率，共振角（反射光强度下降的那个角度）随之移动。</b>⚠ <b>移动量与结合量成正比，所以它给的是一个量、而不只是一个是。代价是要专门的仪器，而且诱饵坐在芯片上、不在细胞里。完整版在速背 09。</b>',
   en:'“Surface plasmon resonance immobilises the bait protein on a dextran layer fixed onto a metal film of nanometre thickness, and a protein mixture is flowed past it. Anything in the mixture that interacts with the bait raises the refractive index at the film surface, and that shifts the resonance angle, the angle at which the reflected light loses intensity. The shift is linear in the amount bound at that spot. It needs no label and no dye, it is fast, and it returns a quantity rather than a yes. The price is a dedicated instrument and a bait sitting on a chip instead of in a cell.”'},
  {r:'高', q:'What is co-immunoprecipitation?',
   ez:'“Co immunoprecipitation asks whether two proteins end up in one pellet. An antibody against the target protein is attached to a solid matrix. The mixture of candidate proteins is added. Anything bound to the target comes down with it. The matrix is then pulled down by gentle spinning. What came down is read on a gel. So the entire readout is whether a band is there. It cannot tell direct contact from a shared complex.”',
   ezcn:'<b>免疫共沉淀（CoIP）＝ 问「两个蛋白会不会落在同一个沉淀里」。</b><b>把认靶蛋白的抗体连到固体基质上，加入待筛蛋白；凡是挂在靶蛋白身上的就跟着一起沉下来，再用低离心力沉淀或微膜过滤，最后在胶上读。</b>⚠ <b>全部读出就是「在不在沉淀里」——它分不出「彼此直接接触」和「同时被第三样东西攒着」。完整版在速背 11 和 13。</b>',
   en:'“Co-immunoprecipitation asks whether two proteins end up in the same pellet. An antibody that specifically recognises the target protein is attached through an affinity reaction to a solid matrix, the candidate proteins are added, and anything that interacts with the target is carried down with it. The matrix is then brought down by low-force centrifugation or caught on a filter, and what came down is read on a gel. The whole readout is whether a band is present. Its blind spot is that being in one pellet does not distinguish direct contact from two proteins held together by a third.”'},
  {r:'高', q:'What is a GST pull-down?',
   ez:'“A GST pull down is affinity purification used as a question. The bait protein is expressed with a glutathione S transferase tag. That tag sticks to glutathione on agarose beads. The candidate protein is incubated with the beads. The beads are spun down and what came with them is read on a gel. One tube holds the tagged bait. A control tube holds the bare tag instead. A band means something only if the control tube is clean.”',
   ezcn:'<b>GST pull-down ＝ 把亲和纯化拿来当问题问。</b><b>诱饵蛋白带上 GST 标签表达，GST 对偶联在琼脂糖球珠上的谷胱甘肽有亲和性；待测蛋白与球珠温育、离心，跟下来的东西在胶上读。</b>⚠ <b>一支管里是带诱饵的标签，另一支对照管里是光杆的标签——条带只有在对照管干净时才有意义。而且它给的是一个百分数，不是一个判决。完整版在速背 14 和 15。</b>',
   en:'“A GST pull-down is affinity purification turned into a question. The bait protein is expressed carrying a glutathione S-transferase tag, and that tag has affinity for glutathione coupled to agarose beads. The candidate protein is incubated with the beads, the beads are spun down, and whatever came with them is read on a gel. One tube holds the tagged bait and a control tube holds the bare tag with the same beads and the same lysate. A band is informative only if the control tube is clean, and the result it gives is a percentage recovered rather than a verdict.”'},
  {r:'高', q:'What is FRET?',
   ez:'“F R E T is energy transfer between two fluorophores. The energy passes without any light being emitted. Three conditions must all hold for it to happen. The two labels must be close, within a few nanometres. Their emission and excitation spectra must overlap. And their dipoles must be oriented suitably. One protein carries cyan fluorescent protein. The other carries yellow fluorescent protein. Transfer shows up as a change in the emitted wavelength.”',
   ezcn:'<b>FRET ＝ 两个荧光基团之间以非辐射方式转移能量（不放出光子）。</b>⚠ <b>三个条件必须同时满足：两个标记足够近（几个纳米之内）、发射与激发光谱重叠、偶极取向合适。</b><b>一个蛋白上接青荧光蛋白，另一个接黄荧光蛋白，结合变近就转移，读出的是发射波长的变化。</b>⚠ <b>没有信号不等于不结合——三个条件缺一个就没信号。完整版在速背 16 和 17。</b>',
   en:'“FRET is fluorescence resonance energy transfer, the passage of energy between two fluorophores without any photon being emitted. Three conditions must hold at once: the two labels must be within a few nanometres of each other, their emission and excitation spectra must overlap, and their dipoles must have a suitable orientation. One protein is tagged with cyan fluorescent protein and the other with yellow, and when they come close the transfer shows up as a change in the emitted wavelength. Its blind spot follows from the three conditions. An absent signal is consistent with two proteins that never bind and also with two that bind in the wrong orientation.”'},
  {r:'高', q:'What is ChIP?',
   ez:'“Ch I P asks where in the genome a protein sits. It stands for chromatin immunoprecipitation. The proteins are first fixed onto the D N A in living cells. The chromatin is then broken into fragments. An antibody against the protein pulls down the fragments it is on. Those fragments are purified and their sequence is read. So the answer is a stretch of chromatin. It is not a single base.”',
   ezcn:'<b>ChIP（染质免疫沉淀）＝ 问「这个蛋白坐在基因组的哪些地方」。</b><b>先在活细胞状态下把蛋白固定到 DNA 上，再把染质打碎成片段，用抗体把带着这个蛋白的片段沉下来、纯化、测序。</b>⚠ <b>所以它给的答案是一段染质，不是一个碱基——分辨率就在那个片段长度上。换一支针对组蛋白修饰的抗体，同一套做法就能测修饰的分布。完整版在速背 18 和 19。</b>',
   en:'“ChIP is chromatin immunoprecipitation, and it asks where in the genome a given protein sits. Proteins are first fixed onto the DNA in living cells, the chromatin is broken into fragments, an antibody against the protein of interest brings down the fragments it is attached to, and those fragments are purified and sequenced. The answer that comes back is a stretch of chromatin of a certain length rather than a single base, so the resolution is set by that fragment size. Swapping in an antibody against a histone modification turns the same procedure into a genome-wide map of that modification.”'},
  {r:'高', q:'What is RNAi used as a method?',
   ez:'“R N A interference used as a method silences one chosen gene. You give the cell a double stranded R N A. Its sequence matches the gene you want silenced. The cell cuts it into small interfering R N As. Those are loaded into a silencing complex. The complex finds the matching message and cuts it. So the cell behaves as if it had lost that gene. But the gene is still in the genome. Only the message was destroyed.”',
   ezcn:'<b>RNAi 当方法用 ＝ 用双链 RNA 把一个选定的基因沉默。</b><b>给细胞一条序列与靶基因同源的双链 RNA，细胞把它切成 siRNA，装进沉默复合物，复合物找到配对的 mRNA 把它切掉。</b>⚠ <b>于是细胞表现得仿佛丢了这个基因——但基因还在基因组里，被毁掉的只是信使。这就是敲低与敲除的区别。完整版在速背 20 到 22。</b>',
   en:'“Used as a method, RNA interference silences one chosen gene. You give the cell a double-stranded RNA whose sequence matches the gene you want silenced. The cell cuts it into small interfering RNAs, and those are loaded into a silencing complex. The complex then finds the matching message and cuts it. The cell then behaves as though it had lost that gene, which is what makes it useful. But the gene is still in the genome and only the message was destroyed, so this is a knockdown and not a knockout.”'},
 ]},
 {g:'⚠ 考官 · Martínková · 构象柔性怎么测（她实验室每天读的数据）', gn:'⚠ <b>2026-09-25 查出来的空白</b>：<b>氢氘交换质谱在全套卡上是 0 格</b>，而它正是 Martínková 实验室看构象变化的主力读数。<b>Prof. Markéta Martínková 做含血红素的气体传感器蛋白</b>：气体结合到血红素铁上 → 构象变 → 分子另一头的功能结构域被打开。<b>她的框架一句话：结合在一端，构象本身就是信号。</b>', items:[
  {r:'高', q:'What does hydrogen–deuterium exchange measure, and which parts of a protein exchange fast?',
    ez:'“It measures how exposed and how flexible the backbone is. Backbone amide hydrogens swap with deuterium from heavy water. A flexible surface loop exchanges fast. It is solvent accessible and no hydrogen bond holds it. A buried beta sheet exchanges slowly. Its amide hydrogen is locked into the hydrogen bond network, and packed side chains keep solvent away. It only exchanges during brief local breathing. So the exchange rate maps flexibility, and a slowed region marks a binding interface.”',
    ezcn:'<b>它测的是骨架有多暴露、有多柔软。</b><b>骨架上的酰胺氢会和重水里的氘对换。</b><b>表面的柔性 loop 换得快</b>：<b>溶剂够得着，而且没有氢键占住它。</b><b>埋在里面的 β 折叠换得慢</b>：<b>它的酰胺氢被氢键网络锁住，周围紧密堆积的侧链又把溶剂隔开，只有在蛋白短暂「呼吸」的瞬间才换得上。</b><b>所以交换速率就是柔性的地图；而某一段变慢了，那里就是结合界面。</b>',
   en:'“It measures how exposed and how flexible the backbone is. Backbone amide hydrogens swap with deuterium from heavy water. A flexible surface loop exchanges fast, because solvent can reach it and no hydrogen bond holds it. A buried beta sheet exchanges slowly, because its amide hydrogen is locked into the hydrogen-bond network and packed side chains keep solvent away, so it only exchanges during brief local breathing. The exchange rate therefore maps flexibility, and a region that slows down on binding marks the interface.”',
   cn:'<b>两句话就够</b>：① 换的是<b>骨架酰胺氢</b>，不是侧链上的氢；② <b>快 = 暴露且没有氢键保护，慢 = 被氢键锁住又被溶剂隔开</b>。<br><b>第三句最值钱</b>：<b>结合之后变慢的那一段就是界面</b> —— 这就是她用它做什么。<span class="pg">通用</span>'},
  {r:'高', q:'A mutation lowers activity. How do you tell a broken active site from a distant allosteric effect?',
    ez:'“I would measure the kinetics and compare with wild type. But I would be careful with one thing. Km is not a binding constant. It is a kinetic constant, and it contains kcat. So a mutation that only damages catalysis can shift Km as well. The cleaner reading is kcat and kcat over Km together. A distant allosteric effect classically lowers kcat and leaves substrate binding nearly alone. To decide properly I would add a conformational probe. Hydrogen deuterium exchange or a fluorescence measurement shows whether regions away from the active site have changed too. If they have, that supports allostery rather than a local break.”',
    ezcn:'<b>我会测动力学跟野生型比，但有一件事要小心：Km 不是结合常数。</b><b>它是动力学常数，里面含着 kcat，所以一个只破坏催化的突变也会把 Km 挪动。</b><b>更干净的读法是 kcat 和 kcat/Km 一起看。</b><b>远端的别构效应典型表现是 kcat 下降而底物结合几乎不变。</b><b>要真判断，我会加一个构象探针</b>：<b>氢氘交换或者荧光，看活性中心以外的区域有没有一起变。</b><b>如果变了，就支持别构而不是局部破坏。</b>',
   en:'“I would measure the kinetics and compare with wild type, but I would be careful about one thing: Km is not a binding constant. It is a kinetic constant and it contains kcat, so a mutation that only damages catalysis can shift Km too. The cleaner reading is kcat and kcat over Km taken together. A distant allosteric effect classically lowers kcat and leaves substrate binding nearly alone. To decide properly I would add a conformational probe, hydrogen–deuterium exchange or fluorescence, and see whether regions away from the active site have changed as well. If they have, that supports allostery rather than a local break.”',
   cn:'⚠ <b>「Km 不是 Kd」这一句是这条的全部价值。</b>她 2026-09-25 那份准备材料在这里把 Km 当成了结合亲和力 —— <b>对着做构象动力学的人说这个，一撬就破。</b><br><b>接卡 02</b>（Kd 与 kon/koff）、<b>19</b>（三类抑制在双倒数图上）、<b>18</b>（活性中心）。<span class="pg">通用</span>'},
  {r:'中', q:'What are a holoenzyme and an apoenzyme, and what if the missing partner is another protein?',
    ez:'“A holoenzyme is the enzyme with everything it needs, so it is fully active. An apoenzyme is the same protein without its cofactor, so activity is lost or much lower. But there is a wording trap. Apoenzyme strictly means a missing non protein cofactor, a coenzyme or a prosthetic group. If the missing partner is another protein subunit, that is not an apoenzyme. That is just the core subunit on its own. Holoenzyme is still fine for a multi subunit complex. D N A polymerase three holoenzyme is the standard example.”',
    ezcn:'<b>全酶 ＝ 该有的都有、活性完整的那个形式。</b><b>脱辅基酶 ＝ 同一个蛋白缺了辅因子，活性丧失或大幅下降。</b>⚠ <b>但这里有个用词陷阱：脱辅基酶严格说指缺了非蛋白的辅因子</b>（辅酶或辅基）。<b>如果缺的是另一条蛋白亚基，那不叫脱辅基酶，那只是「核心亚基单独存在」。</b><b>而「全酶」用在多亚基复合体上是没问题的 —— DNA 聚合酶 III 全酶就是标准例子。</b>',
   en:'“A holoenzyme is the enzyme with everything it needs, so it is fully active, and an apoenzyme is the same protein without its cofactor, so activity is lost or much lower. There is a wording trap, though: apoenzyme strictly means a missing non-protein cofactor, a coenzyme or a prosthetic group. If the missing partner is another protein subunit, that is not an apoenzyme but simply the core subunit on its own. Holoenzyme is still correct for a multi-subunit complex, and DNA polymerase III holoenzyme is the standard example.”',
   cn:'<b>卡 18 和 31 已经有全酶 / 脱辅基酶的定义</b>，这里加的是<b>那个用词边界</b>。<br>⚠ <b>主动说破这条边界是加分</b>：辅因子和亚基不是一回事，而<b>结构域与亚基的区别正是她的第一道题</b>。<span class="pg">通用</span>'}
 ]},

 {g:'定义类 · 他挑一个词问「那是什么」',
  gn:'这些词在前面反复出现。<b>被单独挑出来问的时候，一句话给定义，不要顺着往下讲。</b>',
  items:[
  {r:'高', q:'What is a cis-acting element?',
    ez:'“A cis-acting element is a short D N A sequence. A regulatory protein binds it. It acts on the gene next to it. That gene is on the same molecule of D N A. That is what cis means here.”',
    ezcn:'<b>顺式作用元件 ＝ 一小段 DNA 序列，调控蛋白结合在上面。</b><b>它作用于挨着它的那个基因，而且是同一条 DNA 分子上的</b>——<b>「顺式」指的就是这个。</b>',
    en:'“A cis-acting element is a short DNA sequence that a regulatory protein binds. It acts on the gene it sits next to on the same molecule of DNA.”',
    cn:'「顺式」这个词的意思就是<b>作用在同一条 DNA 上相邻的基因上</b>，跟「反式」相对。<span class="pg">p.219</span>'},
   {r:'高', q:'What is a minimal promoter?',
    ez:'“A minimal promoter is the shortest piece of promoter that still works. Transcription can still start on it. On its own it gives very little. That is why these assays use it. Any reporter signal then comes from the element upstream.”',
    ezcn:'<b>最简启动子 ＝ 还能让转录起始的最短那一段启动子</b>，<b>而它单独存在时几乎什么都给不出来</b>。<b>这些实验用它正是为了这一点：报告基因有信号，那信号就只能来自装在它上游的那个元件。</b>',
    en:'“A minimal promoter is the shortest piece of promoter that still allows transcription to start, and on its own it gives very little. It is used in these assays so that any reporter signal comes from the element placed upstream of it.”',
    cn:'<b>为什么要用最简启动子</b>：背景低。用一个强启动子，报告基因自己就亮了，测不出待测元件的作用。<br><b>它的「核心」具体是什么</b>：转录起始位点 ＋ TATA 盒，上游那些调频率的元件（CAAT 盒、GC 盒）全拿掉了。⚠ <b>这跟 mb-reg 速背 03 的「核心启动子」是同一件事</b>——核心启动子单独起作用时只给基础水平的转录。'},
   {r:'高', q:'What is an activation domain?',
    ez:'“An activation domain recruits the machinery. That machinery starts transcription. The domain does not bind D N A itself. A binding domain is the other half. On its own it binds a promoter region. And it starts nothing.”',
    ezcn:'<b>转录激活结构域负责把启动转录的机器招过来</b>，<b>它自己不结合 DNA</b>。<b>另一半是 DNA 结合结构域</b>：<b>它单独能结合启动子区，但什么也启动不了。</b>',
    en:'“An activation domain is the part of a transcription regulator that recruits the machinery to start transcription. It does not bind DNA itself. A binding domain on its own binds a promoter region and starts nothing.”',
    cn:'<b>两个结构域分工明确</b>：BD 负责定位，AD 负责启动。这张卡上所有酵母方法都建立在这个分工上。<span class="pg">p.221</span>'},
   {r:'中', q:'What does modular mean here?',
  ez:'“Modular means the regulator is built from two or more domains. The domains work independently of each other. So a domain can be taken off one protein. It can be bolted onto another. And it still does its job.”',
  ezcn:'<b>模块化 ＝ 这个调节蛋白是由两个或更多互相独立工作的结构域拼起来的。</b><b>所以一个结构域可以从一个蛋白上拆下来、装到另一个蛋白上，照样干它的活。</b>',
    en:'“Modular means the regulator is built from two or more domains that work independently of each other, so a domain can be taken off one protein and bolted onto another and still do its job.”',
    cn:'这个词是整组酵母方法成立的原因。<b>说清楚 modular，双杂交就不用再解释。</b>'},
   {r:'中', q:'What is a tag?',
  ez:'“A tag is a short peptide stretch fused to a protein. It is chosen for one reason. A ready made antibody or resin recognises it. An H A tag is one common example. A c Myc tag is another.”',
  ezcn:'<b>标签 ＝ 融合在蛋白上的一小段肽，之所以挑它，是因为有现成的抗体或现成的填料认得它。</b><b>常见的两个：HA 标签、c-Myc 标签。</b>',
    en:'“A tag is a short peptide stretch fused to a protein, chosen because a ready made antibody or a ready made resin recognises it. An HA tag and a c-Myc tag are two common ones.”',
    cn:'<b>接卡 pe-pur</b>：那张卡上讲的 His 标签是同一类东西，抓手不同而已。'},
   {r:'中', q:'What is Dicer?',
  ez:'“Dicer is a nuclease with R Nase three activity. It cuts double stranded R N A longer than thirty nucleotides. The pieces it makes are small interfering R N A. Those are twenty one to twenty five nucleotides long.”',
  ezcn:'<b>Dicer ＝ 一个具有 RNase III 活性的核酸酶。</b><b>它把长于 30 个核苷酸的双链 RNA 切成 21–25 个核苷酸的小干扰 RNA。</b>',
    en:'“Dicer is a nuclease with RNase three activity. It cuts double stranded RNA longer than thirty nucleotides into short interfering RNA of twenty one to twenty five nucleotides.”',
    cn:'<b>RNase Ⅲ 活性这个词要带上</b>，它说明 Dicer 切的是双链 RNA 而不是单链。'},
   {r:'中', q:'What is RISC?',
  ez:'“R I S C is the R N A induced silencing complex. It is a ribonucleoprotein. The antisense strand of the small interfering R N A directs its assembly. It then cleaves the target message. It cleaves the region complementary to that strand.”',
  ezcn:'<b>RISC ＝ RNA 诱导的沉默复合物，一个核糖核蛋白。</b><b>它的装配由小干扰 RNA 的反义链引导，随后切开靶 mRNA 上跟那条链互补的那一段。</b>',
    en:'“RISC is the RNA induced silencing complex. It is a ribonucleoprotein assembled under the direction of the antisense strand of the small interfering RNA, and it cleaves the region of the target message complementary to that strand.”',
    cn:'<b>反义链既是向导又是模板</b>：它指导装配，也决定切在哪里。'},
   {r:'中', q:'What is a resonance unit?',
  ez:'“A resonance unit is an arbitrary unit. The shift of the resonance angle is recorded in it. That shift is proportional to one thing. It is proportional to how much material is bound at that spot on the chip.”',
  ezcn:'<b>共振单位 ＝ 记录共振角位移用的那个任意单位。</b><b>那个位移正比于芯片上该点结合了多少物质。</b>',
    en:'“A resonance unit is the arbitrary unit in which the shift of the resonance angle is recorded. It is proportional to the amount of material bound at that spot on the chip.”',
    cn:'⚠ <b>它是相对单位不是摩尔数</b>。书上给的 1000 单位是固定的诱饵量，380 是结合信号的高度。<b>两个数别混。</b>'}
  ]},

 {g:'为什么类 · 他问「为什么是这样」',
  gn:'这一组是<b>卡上给了结论没给理由的地方</b>。他插刀最常插在这里。',
  items:[
   {r:'高', q:'Why does yeast two-hybrid need the two domains on separate proteins?',
    ez:'“Because that is what turns it into a question about two proteins. Suppose both domains were on one polypeptide. Then the reporter would fire regardless. Splitting them changes that. The reporter can fire only if something brings the halves together. And the thing that brings them together is the interaction being tested.”',
    ezcn:'因为<b>这一步才把实验变成「关于两个蛋白的问题」</b>。<b>假如两个结构域长在同一条多肽上，报告基因不管怎样都会亮</b>；<b>拆开之后，只有当某样东西把两半拉到一起时报告基因才亮</b>——<b>而那个「某样东西」正是我们要测的相互作用。</b>',
    en:'“Because that is what turns the assay into a question about two proteins. If both domains were on one polypeptide the reporter would fire regardless. Splitting them means the reporter can only fire if something brings the two halves together, and the thing that brings them together is the interaction being tested.”',
    cn:'<b>这一问答得好不好，直接决定他信不信你懂这个方法。</b>把「为什么要拆开」说成「拆开之后，报告基因亮就等于两个蛋白结合」，逻辑就闭合了。'},
   {r:'高', q:'Why put three or more copies of the element upstream?',
    ez:'“Because more copies raise the efficiency. The factor is recognised and bound more readily. So a weak binder still gives a readable signal. The textbook gives four copies in its worked example.”',
    ezcn:'因为<b>拷贝多了，识别和结合的效率就高</b>——<b>于是一个结合得弱的因子也还能给出读得出来的信号</b>。<b>书的实例里用的是四个拷贝。</b>',
    en:'“Putting three or more copies of the cis-acting element in a row raises the efficiency with which the factor is recognised and bound, so a weak binder still gives a readable reporter signal.”',
    cn:'书上的实例用了 <b>4 个 DRE</b>。<span class="pg">p.220</span><br>⚠ <b>顺带一个隐患</b>：多拷贝也提高了亲合力，所以选出来的可能是弱结合子。<b>这一条书上没写，是从 pe-evo 那张卡上的亲和力/亲合力推过来的通用知识，说的时候标明。</b>'},
   {r:'高', q:'Why is the yeast one-hybrid method worth using at all, when you could purify the protein?',
    ez:'“Because of its sensitivity. It reaches transcription regulators present at very low concentrations. Those concentrations are too low for biochemical purification. That is what the method is for.”',
    ezcn:'因为<b>它灵敏</b>：<b>它够得着那些含量极低、低到任何生化纯化都纯不出来的转录调控因子</b>——<b>这个方法就是为这件事存在的。</b>',
    en:'“Because of its sensitivity. It reaches transcription regulators present at concentrations too low for any biochemical purification to reach. That is what the method is for.”',
    cn:'<b>这一句是书自己写的</b>，而且它回答的正是「为什么不直接纯化」这个最自然的疑问。<span class="pg">p.220</span>'},
   {r:'高', q:'Why must the cells be fixed before the chromatin is cut in a ChIP experiment?',
    ez:'“Because the contact has to be frozen while it still exists. The complexes are fixed while the cells are alive. Only then is the chromatin cut into fragments. Suppose the cells were broken open first. Then the proteins and the D N A would come apart. And nothing could be precipitated.”',
    ezcn:'因为<b>接触必须在它还存在的时候就被冻住</b>。<b>复合物是在细胞还活着的时候固定的，之后才把染色质切成片段</b>。<b>如果先把细胞打开，蛋白和 DNA 就散了，什么也沉不下来。</b>',
    en:'“Because the contact has to be frozen while it still exists. The complexes are fixed while the cells are alive, and only then is the chromatin cut into fragments. If the cells were broken open first, the proteins and the DNA would come apart before anything could be precipitated.”',
    cn:'<b>五步的顺序本身就是答案。</b>顺序反了，实验什么都测不到。'},
   {r:'中', q:'Why is the pull-down done at four degrees?',
  ez:'“Low temperature slows proteolysis in the lysate. It also helps a weak complex. Such a complex is then less likely to come apart. That matters during the incubation and the spin.”',
  ezcn:'<b>低温一来减慢裂解液里的蛋白水解，二来让弱的复合物在孵育和离心过程中不那么容易散开。</b>',
    en:'“Low temperature slows proteolysis in the lysate, and it makes a weak complex less likely to come apart during the incubation and the spin.”',
    cn:'⚠ <b>书上只写了 4 ℃ 这个条件，没写理由。</b>这条是通用知识，说的时候标明。'},
   {r:'中', q:'Why does a short double stranded RNA fail to trigger interference?',
  ez:'“Because it cannot be processed to the right size. Dicer cuts double stranded R N A over thirty nucleotides. It makes pieces of twenty one to twenty five. A duplex too short to be processed cannot mediate interference at all.”',
  ezcn:'因为<b>它没法被加工成合适的大小</b>：<b>Dicer 切的是长于 30 个核苷酸的双链 RNA，产物是 21–25 个核苷酸的片段；短到不能被加工的双链，根本介导不了干扰。</b>',
    en:'“Because it cannot be processed into small interfering RNA of the right size. Dicer cuts double stranded RNA over thirty nucleotides into twenty one to twenty five nucleotide pieces, and a duplex too short to be processed cannot mediate interference at all.”',
    cn:'<b>长度有下限也有上限</b>：在哺乳动物细胞里，太长的 dsRNA 引起非特异沉默。<b>两头都有限制。</b>'}
  ]},

 {g:'⚠ 陷阱 · 说错了听起来还挺对的地方',
  gn:'<b>这一组最值钱。</b>每一条都是「说出来很顺，但把结论说大了一层」。',
  items:[
   {r:'实测', q:'（陷阱）说「CoIP 证明 A 和 B 直接相互作用」',
    ez:'“A co-precipitation shows one thing. The two proteins are in the same complex. I would not call the contact direct. That evidence alone does not show it.”',
    ezcn:'<b>共沉淀只说明一件事：两个蛋白在同一个复合物里。</b>光凭这个证据<b>不能说接触是直接的</b>。要说直接，得用两个纯化蛋白重做 pull-down，或者用 FRET 看距离。',
    en:'“A co-precipitation shows that the two proteins are in the same complex. I would not call the contact direct on that evidence alone.”',
    cn:'<b>正确说法是 in the same complex。</b>这一刀他几乎一定会切，因为它是整组方法里最容易被说大的一个结论。',
    warn:'⚠ 这一条的正确版本<b>书上没写</b>，转录者标了 beyond。说的时候不要挂到书上。'},
   {r:'高', q:'（陷阱）说「没有 FRET 信号说明它们不结合」',
    ez:'“An absent signal proves nothing on its own. It fits two proteins that never bind. It also fits two that bind in an unsuitable orientation. So I cannot conclude they do not interact.”',
    ezcn:'<b>没有信号本身什么也证明不了</b>：<b>它同时符合「两个蛋白从不结合」和「结合了但取向不对」</b>。<b>所以我不能下「它们不相互作用」的结论。</b>',
    en:'“An absent signal is equally consistent with two proteins that never bind and with two that bind in an unsuitable orientation. I cannot conclude they do not interact.”',
    cn:'<b>FRET 测的是几何，不只是接触。</b>距离、光谱重叠、偶极取向，三者缺一就没信号。'},
   {r:'高', q:'（陷阱）说「双杂交阳性说明它们在体内相互作用」',
    ez:'“A hit says one thing. They bind when both are placed in a yeast nucleus. Whether they ever meet in their own cell is a different question. This assay carries no information about that.”',
    ezcn:'<b>一个阳性只说明一件事：这两个蛋白被放进同一个酵母细胞核以后会结合。</b><b>它们在自己原来的细胞里有没有机会相遇，是另一个问题，这个实验对此不含任何信息。</b>',
    en:'“A hit says they bind when both are placed in a yeast nucleus. Whether they ever meet in the cell they came from is not information this assay carries.”',
    cn:'<b>假阳性的来源很具体</b>：原本一个在核里一个在膜上的两个蛋白，被强行放进同一个酵母核。'},
   {r:'高', q:'（陷阱）把 knockdown 说成 knockout',
    ez:'“Interference gives a knockdown. The gene stays in the genome. The message is destroyed instead. So the product is reduced. It is not absent.”',
    ezcn:'<b>RNA 干涉给的是 knockdown</b>：<b>基因还在基因组上，被毁掉的是它的信使</b>——<b>所以产物是「减少」，不是「没有」。</b>',
    en:'“Interference is a knockdown. The gene stays in the genome and the message is destroyed, so the product is reduced rather than absent.”',
    cn:'<b>这两个词说反，等于告诉他你没分清基因和它的信使。</b>'},
   {r:'高', q:'（陷阱）说「蓝色菌落就是阳性结果」',
    ez:'“Blue colonies are picked as positive clones. Every one is then sequenced. And its binding activity is verified separately. So a blue colony is where the verification starts.”',
    ezcn:'<b>蓝色菌落是被当作阳性克隆挑出来的</b>，<b>但每一个还要再测序、再单独验证结合活性</b>——<b>蓝色菌落是验证的起点，不是结论。</b>',
    en:'“Blue colonies are picked as positive clones, and every one is then sequenced and has its binding activity verified separately. A blue colony is where the verification starts.”',
    cn:'<b>书自己写了这一句</b>，所以这一条不用打折。<span class="pg">p.220</span>'},
   {r:'中', q:'（陷阱）把 RNAi 当成一种检测相互作用的方法',
  ez:'“Interference is not a detection method. It is a perturbation method. It does exploit one R N A binding a complementary R N A. But it does not report an interaction.”',
  ezcn:'⚠ <b>RNA 干扰不是检测方法，是扰动方法。</b><b>它确实利用了「一条 RNA 结合另一条互补 RNA」这件事，但它并不报告相互作用。</b>',
    en:'“Interference is not a detection method. It is a perturbation method that exploits an RNA binding a complementary RNA.”',
    cn:'它和前七种<b>不是同一类东西</b>，只是被放在同一节里。<b>主动说清楚这个区别是加分的。</b>'},
   {r:'中', q:'（陷阱）把 SPR 的两个数字说混',
  ez:'“One thousand resonance units is the amount of bait immobilised. That is what was put on the chip. Three hundred and eighty is a different number. It is the height of the binding signal.”',
  ezcn:'⚠ <b>两个数别说混：1000 共振单位是「固定在芯片上的诱饵有多少」；380 是「结合信号的高度」。</b>',
    en:'“One thousand resonance units is how much bait was immobilised on the chip. Three hundred and eighty is the height of the binding signal.”',
    cn:'<b>一个是装了多少，一个是结合了多少。</b>说混了他会追问，而这是个很容易避免的失分。'}
  ]},

 {g:'相邻考点 · 从这道题最容易走到哪儿',
  gn:'他顺着一个词就走了。<b>先知道会走到哪，就不会被带懵。</b>',
  items:[
   {r:'高', q:'（走向 Kd）You mentioned a quantity. What quantity exactly?',
    ez:'“The dissociation constant. It is a concentration of free ligand. At that concentration half the binding sites are occupied. So a lower value means tighter binding. Resonance units and a precipitated percentage both get at it. They get at it experimentally.”',
    ezcn:'<b>解离常数 K<sub>d</sub>。</b><b>它是一个游离配体浓度：在那个浓度下，一半的结合位点被占住</b>——<b>所以数值越小，结合越紧</b>。<b>共振单位和沉降下来的百分比，都是从实验上够到这个量的两种办法。</b>',
    en:'“The dissociation constant. It is the concentration of free ligand at which half of the binding sites are occupied, so a lower value means tighter binding. Resonance units and a precipitated percentage are two ways of getting at it experimentally.”',
    cn:'<b>接卡 02。</b>这是段 4 停止句故意引过来的方向——<b>她在这张卡上是稳的。</b>'},
   {r:'高', q:'（走向纯化）How would you get the purified proteins for that control experiment?',
    ez:'“I would express both as tagged fusions. Then I would purify each one by affinity chromatography. Then I would mix only those two in the tube. So there is no third partner present.”',
    ezcn:'<b>把两个都表达成带标签的融合蛋白，各自用亲和层析纯化出来，然后在管子里只混这两个</b>——<b>这样就没有第三者在场了。</b>',
    en:'“I would express both as tagged fusions and purify each one by affinity chromatography, then mix only those two in the tube so there is no third partner.”',
    cn:'<b>接卡 pe-pur。</b>这一步正是 CoIP 盲点的解法，所以他很可能顺着这里走。'},
   {r:'中', q:'（走向转化）How do you get the two vectors into the yeast?',
  ez:'“By transformation. The bait vector goes in. The prey vectors go in too. Cells that take up both are then selected. The selection is done on the appropriate medium.”',
  ezcn:'<b>靠转化。</b><b>把诱饵载体和猎物载体导入酵母细胞，再在相应的培养基上筛出同时拿到两者的细胞。</b>',
    en:'“By transformation. The bait vector and the prey vectors are introduced into yeast cells, and the cells that take up both are selected on the appropriate medium.”',
    cn:'<b>接卡 14。</b>⚠ <b>酵母是 transformation 不是 transfection</b>——那张卡上把这四个词分清楚了。'},
   {r:'中', q:'（走向表观）What is H3K4me3 and why does it sit at the five prime end?',
  ez:'“It is a methylation on histone H three. It sits on lysine four. It carries three methyl groups. In the cotton experiment the enrichment peaks sit over the five prime ends. That is for two named genes. The gene bodies are near zero. That placement is characteristic of promoter regions. Those promoters belong to actively transcribed genes.”',
  ezcn:'<b>H3K4me3 ＝ 组蛋白 H3 第 4 位赖氨酸上的甲基化，带三个甲基。</b><b>棉花那个实验里，富集峰落在两个被点名基因的 5′ 端，而基因体部分接近零；这种位置分布正是「正在活跃转录的基因」的启动子区域的特征。</b>',
    en:'“It is a methylation on lysine four of histone H3, carried at three methyl groups. In the cotton experiment the enrichment peaks sit over the five prime ends of two named genes with the gene bodies near zero, and that placement is characteristic of the promoter regions of actively transcribed genes.”',
    cn:'<b>这是分子生物学那一门里另一张卡的入口</b>（真核调控与表观）。现在先能说这一句。'},
   {r:'中', q:'（走向敲除）If interference only gives a knockdown, how would you remove the gene completely?',
  ez:'“By gene knockout. The gene is replaced in the chromosome. Homologous recombination does the replacing. It happens between an introduced construct and its matching sequence. Correctly targeted cells are then picked out by selection.”',
  ezcn:'<b>用基因敲除。</b><b>靠导入的构建体跟染色体上与之匹配的序列之间发生同源重组，把那个基因替换掉；随后用选择把正确打靶的细胞挑出来。</b>',
    en:'“By gene knockout. The gene is replaced in the chromosome through homologous recombination between an introduced construct and its matching sequence, and correctly targeted cells are picked out by selection.”',
    cn:'<b>接分子生物学第二张卡</b>（基因敲除、正负双选、CRISPR）。那张卡做出来之前，这一句是她在这个方向上能说的全部。'},
   {r:'中', q:'（走向展示技术）Is a yeast two-hybrid a kind of display?',
  ez:'“They share one idea. Both need a physical link. The link is between a protein and the gene encoding it. That is what lets a hit be recovered and read. In two hybrid the link is the cell. The prey vector is recovered from the colony. In phage display the link is the particle. The protein is outside and its D N A is packaged inside.”',
  ezcn:'<b>它们共享一个想法：都需要「蛋白」和「编码它的基因」之间有一条物理上的连接，这样命中的那一个才能被回收、被读出来。</b><b>双杂交里，连接是那个细胞——猎物载体从菌落里回收；噬菌体展示里，连接是那个颗粒——蛋白在外面，它的 DNA 包在里面。</b>',
    en:'“They share one idea. Both need a physical link between a protein and the gene that encodes it, so that a hit can be recovered and read. In two-hybrid the link is the cell, and the prey vector is recovered from the colony. In phage display the link is the particle, with the protein outside and its DNA packaged inside.”',
    cn:'<b>接卡 pe-evo。</b>这一句把两门课连起来了，说出来很加分——<b>而且这两块她都得学，连起来省一份记忆。</b>'}
  ]},
 {g:'⚠ 书外 · 这张卡上没有、但方法学里绕不过的四种', gn:'出自《现代分子生物学》第五版 <b>p.230–235</b>，<b>捷克书里没有</b>。⚠ <b>2026-09-21 搜过全套 41 张卡：GFP、免疫荧光、体外激酶分析一次都没出现过</b>，EMSA 和 Western 只有一行速查。这四条补的是「它到底怎么做出来的，以及它<b>不</b>说什么」。', items:[
{r:'中', q:'What does a gel shift assay tell you, and what does it not?',
    ez:'“A gel shift assay analyses D N A and protein binding in vitro. Its other name is E M S A. Binding a protein greatly increases the molecular mass of the D N A. In a gel the distance D N A travels toward the positive electrode falls with mass. So free probe runs fast and reaches the bottom. Complexed probe is retarded and stops higher up. Where it stops on the gel is the whole measurement. The probe D N A is labelled, usually with phosphorus thirty two. The protein is never labelled. A cell extract holds thousands of different proteins. Labelling protein would label all of them. The film would report where the proteins went. With the label on the probe every band is one molecule. The gel is non denaturing so the complex survives. The assay never says which protein bound.”',
    ezcn:'<b>凝胶滞缓实验（EMSA）＝ 体外分析 DNA 与蛋白质相互作用的一种凝胶电泳技术。</b><b>原理：蛋白质与 DNA 结合后大大增加相对分子质量，而电泳中 DNA 朝正电极移动的距离与其相对分子质量的对数成反比——<b>没结合蛋白的片段跑得快，形成了复合物的受到阻滞跑得慢</b>；于是「在胶上跑到哪里」就是全部的测量。</b><b>做法：用 ³²P 标记探针 DNA，与细胞提取物共温育让复合物形成，加到<b>非变性</b>聚丙烯酰胺凝胶中电泳（非变性指这种胶不让蛋白质变性，复合物因此保持完整），最后放射自显影。</b>⚠ <b>为什么标 DNA 不标蛋白：细胞提取物里有成千上万种蛋白，标记打在蛋白上就等于把它们全标上了，胶片报告的将是「蛋白质跑到哪里」；标记由探针携带，胶片上每一条带就都是同一个分子——胶片只需要回答一个问题：这一个分子最后停在哪里。</b>⚠ <b>它不说出结合上去的是哪一个蛋白，这正是它被当作分离纯化该蛋白第一步的原因。</b>',
 en:'“A gel shift assay, or electrophoretic mobility shift assay, is a special gel electrophoresis technique for analysing the interaction between DNA and protein in vitro. Binding a protein greatly increases the molecular mass of the DNA, and in gel electrophoresis the distance DNA travels toward the positive electrode depends on the logarithm of its molecular mass. A DNA fragment with no protein bound migrates fast and ends near the bottom. A fragment that has formed a DNA-protein complex is retarded and stops higher up. Where the band stops on the gel is the whole of the measurement. The probe DNA is labelled, usually with phosphorus thirty-two, and the protein is never labelled. The reason is simple. A cell extract contains thousands of different proteins, so labelling protein would label all of them and the film would report where the proteins went. With the label on the probe, every band on the film is the same one molecule, and the film only has to answer where that molecule stopped. The gel is non-denaturing, so the complex stays intact during the run. What the assay never tells you is which protein in the extract did the binding, and that is exactly why it is used as the first step in purifying that protein.”',
 cn:'<b>p.230–231，图 6-34</b>。<b>历史</b>：这项技术首次为大肠杆菌乳糖阻遏物与其 DNA 结合位点的相互作用提供了动态数据（接卡 12）。<b>书上的例子</b>：取棉花乙烯合成酶 ACO3 基因上游启动子，划成 PⅠ～PⅥ 六个区段，在亚洲棉与雷蒙德棉之间比较，每段各作 γ-³²P 标记探针；<b>只有 PⅡ 这一组在胶上部出现明显滞缓条带</b>，其余各道底部只有自由探针——而 <b>MYB 结合位点恰好画在 PⅡ 这一段里</b>。⚠ <b>滞缓把结合定位到启动子的某一个亚区段，然后就停住了。</b>'},
{r:'中', q:'What is an in-gel kinase assay?',
    ez:'“An in gel kinase assay measures kinase activity outside the cell. A protein kinase moves the gamma phosphate of A T P onto a substrate. The acceptor is a serine, a threonine or a tyrosine residue. A protein phosphatase runs the reverse reaction. A cell may hold up to a thousand different kinases. So measuring one of them inside a living cell is very hard. The assay is therefore moved into a tube. You purify the protein you want to test. You run it into a gel that already contains a substrate protein. The substrate is myelin basic protein. Many kinases can phosphorylate it. After the run you soak the gel in labelled A T P. Any protein with kinase activity phosphorylates the substrate around itself. The film then shows a band where that kinase stopped.”',
    ezcn:'<b>体外激酶活性分析 ＝ 把「这个蛋白有没有激酶活性」的测定搬到细胞外面做。</b><b>蛋白激酶催化 ATP 或 GTP 的 γ 磷酸基团转移到底物蛋白的丝氨酸、苏氨酸或酪氨酸残基上；蛋白磷酸酯酶催化相反的去磷酸化。</b>⚠ <b>为什么要搬出来：细胞内可能有多达上千个蛋白激酶，在活细胞里检测其中任何一个的活性都非常困难。</b><b>两步：① 获取底物蛋白和待检测的激酶（目的蛋白可直接从组织提取，也可由表达载体诱导表达后分离纯化）；② 在细胞之外进行磷酸化反应。</b><b>具体做法：把纯化好的蛋白加到一块<b>预先均匀混入底物蛋白</b>的聚丙烯酰胺凝胶中电泳——底物用<b>髓鞘碱性蛋白（MBP）</b>，一种许多激酶都能使之磷酸化的小蛋白——电泳后把胶浸在含 <b>γ-³²P–ATP</b> 的反应体系里，凡是具有激酶活性的蛋白，都会把这个被标记的磷酸基团转移到它自己所在位置周围的 MBP 上；之后胶内复性、干胶、放射自显影。</b>⚠ <b>胶片上的黑带落在激酶本身停在胶上的那个位置。</b>',
 en:'“An in-gel kinase assay measures kinase activity outside the cell. A protein kinase catalyses transfer of the gamma phosphate group of ATP or GTP onto a serine, threonine or tyrosine residue of a substrate protein, and a protein phosphatase catalyses the reverse. A cell may contain up to a thousand different protein kinases. Detecting the activity of any one of them inside a living cell is therefore very difficult, and that is why the measurement is moved into a tube. There are two stages. First you obtain the substrate protein and the kinase to be tested, either extracted from tissue directly or expressed from a vector and purified. Second you run the phosphorylation reaction outside the cell. In practice the purified protein is run into a polyacrylamide gel that already has a substrate protein mixed evenly through it. The substrate used is myelin basic protein, a small protein that many kinases can phosphorylate. After the run the gel is soaked in a reaction mixture containing ATP labelled with phosphorus thirty-two on the gamma phosphate. Any protein with kinase activity transfers that labelled phosphate onto the substrate around its own position in the gel. The gel is then renatured, dried and autoradiographed, and the dark band on the film falls exactly where the kinase itself stopped.”',
 cn:'<b>p.232–233，图 6-36、图 6-37</b>。<b>书上的例子</b>：把棉花钙依赖性蛋白激酶 <b>GhCDPK1</b> 与棉花乙烯合成酶 <b>GhACS2</b> 放进同一个体外磷酸化体系——<b>只有两个蛋白同时存在的泳道才出现很强的条带，加入 EGTA（一种螯合剂，能把钙离子攥住拿走）之后条带明显减弱</b>；同一个激酶对 GhSUS 和 GhACO1 则完全不磷酸化。⚠ <b>结论的边界</b>：试管里跑出来的说明「有钙时 GhCDPK1 能磷酸化 GhACS2」，<b>至于活细胞里是否真的发生，恰恰是当初把测定赶出细胞的那个问题</b>。（图 6-36 中泳道 1、4、5 在 Mr 68 000 附近出现条带，泳道 2、3、6 一片空白。）'},
{r:'中', q:'How do you find out where a protein sits inside a cell?',
    ez:'“Two methods answer that, and they differ in one way. Green fluorescent protein gives an address by construction. G F P has two hundred thirty eight amino acids. It has two absorption peaks and two emission peaks. The emitted light is green or yellow green. You can build two kinds of construct with it. Joining G F P to the promoter of your gene gives a chimeric gene. Joining G F P to the coding sequence gives a fusion protein. A construct driven by the gene own control elements copies that gene pattern. So wherever G F P lights up, the target protein should be. Immunofluorescence answers the same question differently. A fluorescent antibody serves as the probe. It needs no transformation and no fusion construct. It reads the unmodified protein where it really is.”',
    ezcn:'<b>两种读法，分别在一件事上不同。</b><b>① <b>GFP</b>（绿色荧光蛋白，238 个氨基酸；主吸收峰 395 nm 由紫外激发，另一个 475 nm 由蓝光激发；发射峰 509 nm 和 540 nm，绿或黄绿色荧光）。可以构建两种东西：<b>把 GFP 编码序列与目的基因的启动子融合 → 嵌合基因</b>；<b>把 GFP 编码序列与目的蛋白的编码序列直接相连 → 融合基因</b>。转入方法有花序浸染、基因枪、显微注射、愈伤组织转化、细胞转染。</b>⚠ <b>由目的基因自己的表达调控元件驱动的构建，表达模式与该基因相同；于是荧光显微镜下 GFP 出现在哪里，目的蛋白就该在哪里</b>（图 6-39：WOX5pro::GFP 亮在拟南芥根尖的静止中心）。<b>② <b>免疫荧光</b> ＝ 把抗原抗体特异结合与荧光标记结合：用荧光标记的抗体作分子探针检测细胞或组织内的相应抗原；实际操作中荧光素更常挂在识别一抗的<b>二抗</b>上。</b>⚠ <b>免疫荧光不需要转化、也不需要融合构建，它读的是未经改动的蛋白质本来所在的位置。</b>',
 en:'“Two methods answer that question, and they differ in one important way. The first is green fluorescent protein, which gives an address by construction. GFP is made of two hundred and thirty-eight amino acids. It has two absorption peaks. The main one is at three hundred and ninety-five nanometres, excited by ultraviolet light, and the second at four hundred and seventy-five, excited by blue light. It also has two emission peaks, at five hundred and nine and five hundred and forty, so the fluorescence is green or yellow-green. Two kinds of construct can be built from it. Joining the GFP coding sequence to the promoter of your gene gives a chimeric gene. Joining it directly to the coding sequence of your protein gives a fusion gene. A construct driven by the target gene own regulatory elements has the same expression pattern as that gene, so wherever GFP appears under the fluorescence microscope is where the target protein should be. The second method is immunofluorescence, which combines specific antigen-antibody binding with fluorescent labelling. A fluorescently labelled antibody acts as the probe for the corresponding antigen in a cell or tissue, and in practice the fluorophore is usually carried on the secondary antibody. Immunofluorescence needs no transformation and no fusion construct. It reads the unmodified protein where it actually is.”',
 cn:'<b>p.229, p.235，图 6-39、图 6-40</b>。⚠ <b>两句边界要一起说</b>：<b>荧光落在某个亚细胞区域，这句话只关于定位——它给了基因产物一个细胞内的地址，而这个产物的生化功能仍然完全没有交代。</b><b>免疫荧光的例子</b>：用结核杆菌外膜蛋白刺激巨噬细胞 15 min——0 min 时 NF-κB（FITC 标记）的荧光呈环状包绕在核外的胞质中，<b>15 min 后它的信号与 DAPI 标记的核 DNA 重合</b>；⚠ <b>15 分钟之内一个蛋白从胞质进入细胞核，正是它让你看见的东西</b>（接 mb-reg 和 mb-post 的信号转导那一层）。'},
{r:'中', q:'What does a Western blot prove?',
    ez:'“A Western blot decides whether a sample contains a given protein antigen. It rests on one property of antibodies. The protein binds only its own labelled specific antibody. That binding does not change its mass in the gel. The procedure has five steps. You prepare the protein sample. You separate it by S D S P A G E. You transfer the separated proteins onto a membrane. You then block the unreacted sites on that membrane. You bind an unlabelled primary antibody to the protein. You wash and add a labelled secondary antibody. Colour or autoradiography then reveals the band. The two antibodies do one job together. They deliver a signal making enzyme to an unlabelled protein. A band at the expected place says two things only. The sample holds a protein of that size. That protein reacts with this antibody.”',
    ezcn:'<b>蛋白质免疫印迹（Western blotting）＝ 判定样品中有没有某种蛋白抗原的技术</b>（20 世纪 70 年代末 80 年代初，在蛋白质凝胶电泳和固相免疫测定的基础上发展起来）。<b>原理只是抗体的一条性质：被测蛋白只能与标记的特异性抗体相结合，而这种结合不改变它在凝胶电泳中的相对分子质量。</b><b>五步：① 蛋白质样品制备；② SDS-PAGE 分离；③ 转移到尼龙或其他膜上，转移后先把膜上未反应的位点<b>封闭</b>起来，抑制抗体的非特异性吸附；④ 用膜上固定的蛋白作抗原，与非标记的<b>一抗</b>结合；⑤ 洗去未结合的一抗，加酶偶联或同位素标记的<b>二抗</b>，显色或放射自显影检出。</b>⚠ <b>一前一后两支抗体的作用，是把一个能产生信号的酶送到一个自身不带任何标记的蛋白身上</b>（图 6-38：辣根过氧化物酶挂在二抗上，把无色的 DAB 底物变成深色产物）。⚠ <b>出现在预期位置的一条带只说两件事：样品里有这个大小的蛋白，并且它与这支抗体起反应。它不说这个蛋白有没有功能，也不说它原来待在细胞的什么地方。</b>',
 en:'“A Western blot decides whether a sample contains a particular protein antigen. It was developed at the end of the nineteen seventies on the basis of protein gel electrophoresis and solid-phase immunoassay, and it rests on a single property of antibodies. The protein being measured binds only its own labelled specific antibody, and that binding does not change the molecular mass it shows in gel electrophoresis. The procedure has five steps. You prepare the protein sample. You separate it by SDS-PAGE. You transfer the separated proteins onto a nylon or other membrane and then block the unreacted sites on the membrane, so that antibodies cannot adsorb non-specifically. You use the proteins fixed on the membrane as antigen and bind an unlabelled primary antibody to them. Finally you wash away the unbound primary antibody, add an enzyme-coupled or radioactively labelled secondary antibody, and detect the result by colour development or autoradiography. The two antibodies together do one job. They deliver an enzyme that can generate a signal to a protein that carries no label of its own. A band at the expected position says only two things. The sample contains a protein of that size, and that protein reacts with this antibody. It says nothing about whether the protein has any function, and nothing about where in the cell it used to be.”',
 cn:'<b>p.234–235，图 6-38</b>。<b>影响成败的两个因素</b>：① <b>表位（epitope）的性质</b>——所选一抗必须能识别<b>经电泳变性、并转印固定到膜上</b>的蛋白，而且不能与膜上别的东西交叉反应；⚠ <b>正因如此，免疫印迹同时也是评价一支新抗体特异性的好办法</b>。② <b>抗原浓度</b>——对相对分子质量 5×10⁴ 左右的蛋白，浓度需 <b>大于 0.1 ng</b> 才能检出，低于此值必须先进一步纯化再上样。'},
 ]},
 {g:'怎么发现的', gn:'⚠ <b>2026-09-21 补的一组</b>（`tools/askgroups.py` 查出来这张卡缺它）。<b>除了标了书页的那一行，其余全是通用知识，说的时候标 general。</b>⚠ <b>年份不确定的地方标了「待核」，别当确定的数报出去。</b>', items:[
{r:'中', q:'How was the two-hybrid assay invented?',
    ez:'“It came out of a fact about transcription factors. Such a factor has two separable parts. One is a D N A binding domain. The other is an activation domain. They were shown to work while on two different molecules. Something else only has to hold them together. That is the whole idea of the assay. You put the bait on the binding domain. You put the prey on the activation domain. Bait and prey bind. The two domains are then held together. The reporter gene then fires. Fields and Song built it in nineteen eighty nine. So the reason it works is not about the assay. It is a fact about transcription factors.”',
    ezcn:'⚠ <b>它是从一个关于<b>转录因子</b>的事实里长出来的：一个转录因子有两个<b>可以分开</b>的部件——<b>DNA 结合域</b>和<b>转录激活域</b>；而实验证明，这两个部件<b>即使长在两个不同的分子上，只要有东西把它们拉到一起，照样工作</b>。</b><b>这就是整个测定的全部想法：诱饵接在结合域上，猎物接在激活域上；两者一结合，两个结构域就被牵到一起，报告基因点着。</b><b>Fields 与 Song，1989 年。</b>⚠ <b>所以「它为什么成立」这个问题的答案不在这个方法身上，而是关于转录因子的一个事实。</b>',
 en:'“It came out of a fact about transcription factors rather than out of a method. Such a factor has two separable parts, a DNA-binding domain and an activation domain, and they were shown to work even while sitting on two different molecules, provided something else holds them together. That is the whole idea of the assay. The bait goes on the binding domain and the prey goes on the activation domain. If bait and prey bind, the two domains are held together and the reporter gene fires. Fields and Song built it in nineteen eighty-nine. So the reason the assay works is not a fact about the assay at all. It is a fact about transcription factors.”',
 cn:'⚠ <b>这一条把这张卡的两组接上了</b>：术语表里的「DNA 结合域 · 转录激活域 · 组件式」是名词，这一条是那几个名词<b>为什么能拆开用</b>。<b>通用知识，标 general</b>；1989 这个年份是安全的。'},
{r:'中', q:'What did the gel shift assay first show?',
    ez:'“It first gave dynamic data for one pair. The pair was the lac repressor and its operator D N A. Before it the binding was inferred from genetics. The assay made it visible on a gel. Free probe runs to the bottom. Bound probe is retarded and stops higher. So a binding event became a band position. That is why the method spread so fast. It converts an invisible interaction into a distance. And it explains the limit at the same time. The gel says something bound. It never says which protein bound.”',
    ezcn:'<b>它最早给出动态数据的那一对是：<b>大肠杆菌乳糖阻遏物与它的操纵基因 DNA</b>。</b><b>在它之前，这个结合是从遗传学<b>推</b>出来的；这个方法把它<b>在胶上变成看得见的东西</b>：自由探针跑到底部，结合了的被阻滞、停在更高的位置。</b>⚠ <b>于是一次结合事件变成了一个条带位置——这正是这个方法传播得这么快的原因：<b>它把一个看不见的相互作用换算成了一段距离</b>。</b>⚠ <b>同一句话也说出了它的界限：胶告诉你「有东西结合了」，它从不告诉你「结合的是哪一个蛋白」。</b>',
 en:'“It first gave dynamic data for one particular pair, the lac repressor and its operator DNA. Before that the binding had been inferred from genetics rather than watched. The assay made it visible on a gel, because free probe runs to the bottom while bound probe is retarded and stops higher up. So a binding event became a band position, and that is why the method spread so quickly. It converts an invisible interaction into a distance. The same sentence states its limit. The gel tells you that something bound, and it never tells you which protein bound.”',
 cn:'<b>通用知识，标 general。</b>⚠ <b>跟卡 12 的接口就在这里</b>：那张卡讲 lac 操纵子的机制，而<b>这个方法最早测的就是它</b>。这一条跟书外那组的 EMSA 那一条连着说，一条讲怎么来的、一条讲怎么做的。'},
 ]}
]
});
